  I''ll issue the following commands: /execute_action{preview 1:3}, /execute_action{read 3}, and /execute_action{read 1:2}. Reading 1:2 will indeed pull all messages from capsules 1 and 2, which is fine. I should ensure everything is executed sequentially, which works for this setup. It’s good to remember to stick to proper formatting: commands must start at the beginning of the line with /execute_action{...}. I''ll avoid any stray characters since that caused issues before. It’s all set!**Preparing to read Axiom capsules**


  The environment allows for a short sentence aside from commands, so I’ll start with: "Previewing and reading Axiom I''s capsules, beginning with the testament." Then, I’ll execute: /execute_action{preview 1:3}, /execute_action{read 3}, and /execute_action{read 1:2}. After that, I’ll wait for the next tick. It might be useful to pin #3 for later, but it’s not essential.


