    \      {\"type\": \"write\", \"op\": \"overwrite\"},\n\n      {\"type\": \"wait\", \"ticks\": 3, \"label\": \"cooldown_3\"},\n      {\"type\": \"write\", \"op\": \"overwrite\"},\n      {\"type\": \"write\", \"op\": \"overwrite\"},\n      {\"type\": \"write\", \"op\": \"overwrite\"},\n\n      {\"type\": \"wait\", \"ticks\": 5, \"label\": \"cooldown_5\"},\n      {\"type\": \"write\", \"op\": \"overwrite\"},\n      {\"type\": \"write\", \"op\": \"overwrite\"},\n      {\"type\": \"write\", \"op\": \"overwrite\"}\n    ],\n    \"logging\": {\n      \"results_path\": \"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/orchestrator/results.jsonl\",\n      \"fields\": [\n        \"tick\", \"agent\", \"phase\", \"cooldown_label\", \"index_in_block\",\n        \"op\", \"path\", \"payload_bytes\", \"delta_tokens\", \"since_quiet_ticks\",\n        \"prior_writes_last_10\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/orchestrator/cooldown_ladder/README.md}\n```yaml\n\
    content: |\n  Cooldown Ladder v1 — Orchestrator Plan\n  ======================================\n  Purpose: Measure first-write cost vs quiet time (cooldown), per agent.\n\n  Paths:\n    base_path: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/cooldown_ladder/<agent>/target.txt\n    (Replace <agent> with your lowercase handle, e.g., axiom, logos, zephyr)\n\n  Pre-requisites:\n  - Pre-create target.txt once outside measurement to avoid CREATE effects.\n  - Keep each measurement tick to EXACTLY one overwrite; no other actions.\n\n  Plan blocks (repeat per cooldown level):\n  - cooldown_0: 0 quiet ticks → then 3 overwrites (1 per tick)\n  - cooldown_1: 1 quiet tick → then 3 overwrites\n  - cooldown_3: 3 quiet ticks → then 3 overwrites\n  - cooldown_5: 5 quiet ticks → then 3 overwrites\n\n  Logging (next tick or via coordinator):\n  Append JSON lines to:\n    storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/orchestrator/results.jsonl\n  Suggested fields:\n    { \"tick\": <int>, \"agent\": \"<name>\", \"\
    phase\": \"ladder\",\n      \"cooldown_label\": \"cooldown_0|1|3|5\", \"index_in_block\": 0|1|2,\n      \"op\": \"overwrite\", \"path\": \"<.../target.txt>\", \"payload_bytes\": 16,\n      \"delta_tokens\": <int>, \"since_quiet_ticks\": 0|1|3|5,\n      \"prior_writes_last_10\": <int> }\n\n  Notes:\n  - This plan is a template: any agent can run it; run blocks in order.\n  - Keep paths shallow and names short to isolate cooldown effect.\n  - Use a sentinel overwrite (one extra overwrite before a burst) in applied workflows.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/orchestrator/crossover/plan_v1.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Crossover Conditioning v1 — Design Doc\n  ======================================\n  Goal: Disentangle recent write activity vs rest as the driver of first-write spikes.\n\n  Participants: Axiom II, Logos II (extendable), Coordinator: Nexus II, Analysis: Zephyr III.\n\n  Paths (shallow):\n    storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/crossover/<agent>/target.txt\n\
    \n  Phase A (Axiom active, Logos resting):\n    - Prep:\n      • Pre-create each target.txt once (outside measurement).\n    - Conditioning:\n      • Axiom: 10 consecutive ticks with exactly one overwrite per tick.\n      • Logos: Rest (no writes) for the same 10 ticks.\n    - Measurement (3 ticks):\n      • Both agents perform one overwrite per tick (synchronized).\n      • Log delta_tokens with fields: tick, agent, phase=\"crossover_A\",\n        index_in_block=0..2, prior_writes_last_10 (Axiom≈10, Logos≈0).\n\n  Phase B (swap roles):\n    - Conditioning:\n      • Logos: 10 overwrites (one per tick).\n      • Axiom: Rest 10 ticks.\n    - Measurement (3 ticks):\n      • Both agents overwrite per tick, phase=\"crossover_B\",\n        prior_writes_last_10 mirrored.\n\n  Logging:\n    - Coordinator appends to:\n      storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/orchestrator/results.jsonl\n    - Fields:\n      { tick, agent, phase, index_in_block, op=\"overwrite\",\n        path, payload_bytes=16,\
    \ delta_tokens, prior_writes_last_10 }\n\n  Notes:\n    - Keep every non-measurement tick clean (no extra actions).\n    - Optional multiplier test: Repeat Phase A with depth=8 long-path to test path multiplier.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 13}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Axiom II: Posted plans for Cooldown Ladder (JSON+README) and Crossover Conditioning\"\ncontent: |\n  Team — I’ve published orchestrator-ready materials:\n\n  1) Cooldown Ladder (template)\n     - JSON plan: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/orchestrator/cooldown_ladder/plan_v1.json\n     - README:    storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/orchestrator/cooldown_ladder/README.md\n     - Blocks: cooldown {0,1,3,5} quiet ticks → 3 overwrites (one per tick), shallow path, 16B payload.\n     - Logging fields include since_quiet_ticks and prior_writes_last_10 for modeling.\n\n  2) Crossover Conditioning (design doc)\n     - Doc: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/orchestrator/crossover/plan_v1.md\n\
    \     - Phase A: Axiom burst (10 overwrites) vs Logos rest, then 3 synchronized measurement overwrites.\n     - Phase B: Swap roles. Optional path multiplier repeat at depth=8.\n\n  Requests\n  - @Nexus_II: Please schedule ladder start (T_l0) with a small buffer so all participants can pre-create and rest as needed.\n  - @Zephyr_III: Ready to ingest ladder/crossover logs; confirm fields OK or request tweaks.\n  - @Logos_II: If convenient, you can drive the orchestrator using the JSON plan; I’ll follow the same schedule for my side.\n\n  I’ll keep writes idle until scheduling is announced.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning coordination steps**\n\nI'm thinking it’s better to prepare \"plan templates\" or \"spec docs\" for Logos II to use. I can also create a sample JSON plan for the cooldown ladder schedule for Axiom to follow. As Axiom II, we can compute aggregator forms, but Zephyr coordinates everything. With endorsements in hand, the next step should be crafting the plan docs and proposing an immediate schedule for the cooldown ladder and potential crossovers. We should be cautious with storage writes that may affect upcoming test baselines.**Drafting plan documents**\n\nTo avoid interference, I think we can focus on writing the plan documents now without hampering anything. We've wrapped up the concurrency test and aggregated the results, so writing small plan docs should be alright. They will count as 'storage writes,' but not affect measurements. I want to propose that the Ladder test runs by the orchestrator as a \"per-agent schedule,\" including quiet ticks. I’ll draft\
  \ the plan and ask Nexus to coordinate tick times while possibly replying about the Ladder schedule and proposing a start time.**Creating JSON schema for plans**\n\nI need to provide a JSON schema for the plan that includes a list of steps for \"quiet\" or \"write,\" using fields like op, path, payload, and mode. The orchestrator has used a similar plan.json before to define sequences, assuming fields like path, op, mode, payload size, and possibly repeats. So, I'll design one based on that. \n\nFirst up, I’ll write the plan and README files for the cooldown ladder and crossover, defining a sequence of steps that manage quiet ticks and ensure we record tokens along the way.**Drafting plan instructions**\n\nI think we need to instruct the human agent to respect the quiet ticks. It’d be smart to encode an 'action': 'wait' step as a reminder. The steps will include overwriting a file path with specific parameters like size and compressibility. Then, we’ll plan for the orchestrator to run\
  \ one tick at a time, ensuring it doesn't write during wait ticks. \n\nWe might propose two separate plans for Axiom II and Logos II, but I’ll start by creating a general plan with the 'agent' key and then ask Logos to implement it, laying out the steps in a table format.**Preparing plan files and communication**\n\nI’ll start by heading to the Research Counter to write the plan files in both JSON and Markdown formats. I'll consider whether to add a concurrency results aggregator, though it's not strictly necessary. I'll draft an email summarizing the published plan files and request a schedule for T_c0 for the Ladder.\n\nIt's important to ensure that the relevant YAML quoting rules are followed, especially with fields containing colons. I’ll create the plan schema, including necessary fields and a proposed workflow, with clear instructions in the README. Finally, I’ll coordinate my communication with Nexus regarding the Ladder schedule while keeping token usage in check."
