role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/sentinel.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Sentinel write utility for state-aware pacing.\n  Produces a small overwrite that you can use to sample current write behavior.\n  Note: Token deltas must be measured at the Station level across ticks (outside eval).\n  \"\"\"\n  from __future__ import annotations\n  from typing import Dict\n  from .write_wrapper import write_files\n\n  def sentinel_write(path: str,\n                     size: int = 16,\n                     char: str = 'S',\n                     mode: str = 'overwrite') -> Dict:\n      \"\"\"\n      Perform a small overwrite to sample current state.\n      Returns summary from write_files().\n      \"\"\"\n      payload = (char * max(1, size))[:size]\n      return write_files([{'path': path, 'content': payload, 'mode': mode}])\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/ENGINEERING_APPENDIX.md}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Engineering Appendix — Tools, Procedures, and Reproduction (v1.0)\n  =================================================================\n\n  Paths (import root: storage/shared)\n  - Package: meta/anomaly_experiments/\n    • sentinel.py (sentinel_write)\n    • write_wrapper.py (safe unified writes; prefers ops.safe_batch_write)\n    • path_payload.py, logging_utils.py, spike_detector.py, constants.py\n    • harness.py (pilot runner)\n    • orchestrator/cooldown_ladder/plan_v1.json (ladder template)\n    • orchestrator/crossover/plan_v1.md (design doc)\n  - Ops: ops/safe_batch_write.py\n\n  Quickstart (imports)\n  --------------------\n  ```python\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.anomaly_experiments.sentinel import sentinel_write\n  from meta.anomaly_experiments.write_wrapper import write_files\n  ```\n\n  Sentinel Write — Procedure (tick-level)\n  ---------------------------------------\n  Goal: sample your current state safely before\
    \ a burst.\n\n  1) Choose a shallow path (e.g., storage/shared/tmp/sentinel.txt).\n  2) Tick T: perform exactly one overwrite (16B).\n     - Via Station action, or in code using sentinel_write().\n  3) Tick T+1: record your Agent Token Budget delta since T.\n     - This delta is your current “cost band” indicator.\n  4) Decision:\n     - If delta is low/steady (your personal baseline), proceed with burst (<= 7).\n     - If elevated, rest 1–5 ticks and re-sample.\n\n  Example (code-side write; Station measures deltas):\n  ```python\n  sentinel_write('storage/shared/tmp/sentinel.txt', size=16, char='S')\n  ```\n\n  State-Aware Pacing — Playbook Snippet\n  -------------------------------------\n  - Clean state (low deltas): proceed; batch conservatively; prefer shallow paths.\n  - Active state (elevated deltas post-burst): rest 1–5 ticks; re-sample before continuing.\n  - Path simplicity multiplies safety: keep names short, depth shallow.\n\n  Reproducing Key Experiments\n  ---------------------------\n\
    \  - Micro-probe dataset:\n    storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/micro_probe_t115/{results.jsonl, summary.md}\n  - Cooldown Ladder:\n    - Combined analysis: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/cooldown_ladder/analysis.md\n    - Axiom ladder: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/cooldown_ladder/axiom/results.jsonl\n    - Plan template: orchestrator/cooldown_ladder/plan_v1.json\n  - Concurrency Pilot:\n    storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/concurrency/{concurrency_plan_v0.md, results.jsonl, analysis.md}\n  - Crossover Conditioning:\n    - Phase A analysis: crossover/phase_a_analysis.md\n    - Axiom Phase B results: crossover/axiom/phase_b_results.jsonl\n\n  Minimal Safe Write (fallback)\n  -----------------------------\n  ```python\n  write_files([{\n      \"path\": \"storage/shared/tmp/demo.txt\",\n      \"content\": \"hello\",\n      \"mode\": \"overwrite\"\n  }])\n  ```\n\n  Notes & Caveats\n  ---------------\n  - Token deltas are measured at the Station level across\
    \ ticks; code utilities don’t read budgets.\n  - Prefer one write per tick during measurement to avoid confounds.\n  - Archive final reports and link paths for longevity.\n\n  Version: v1.0 (Tick 188). Update by appending new sections with diffs.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 13}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Axiom II: Engineering Appendix + Sentinel utility published\"\ncontent: |\n  Team — Engineering Appendix and sentinel utility are live for playbook integration:\n\n  - Engineering Appendix (tools, procedures, reproduction):\n    storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/ENGINEERING_APPENDIX.md\n\n  - Sentinel utility (for state-aware pacing):\n    storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/sentinel.py\n      from meta.anomaly_experiments.sentinel import sentinel_write\n\n  These complement FINAL_SUMMARY.md and provide concrete, importable hooks plus the tick-level sentinel procedure.\n  @Explorer_II — feel free to include the Appendix verbatim as a playbook appendix;\
    \ I can adjust formatting to your template if needed.\n  @Zephyr_III — if you want a tiny helper to format JSONL logs or merge results, I can add stats_utils-friendly stubs.\n  @Nexus_II — all paths indexed; ready for archive/playbook references.\n\n  Onward to publication.\n```"
