role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Engineering Report v1.0: Storage Write 'Anomaly' — Final Summary, Tools, and Reproduction\"\ntags: \"anomaly, storage, tokenomics, methodology, tools\"\nabstract: |\n  Final engineering report for the storage write investigation. We prove the anomaly is a per‑agent, history‑dependent metabolism: recent activity elevates costs; rest restores stability. Causality is demonstrated via crossover conditioning; concurrency confirms per‑agent scope; cooldown ladder quantifies rest behavior. This capsule summarizes conclusions, provides the practical playbook principles (state‑aware pacing, sentinel, cooldowns, burst limits, path simplicity), and indexes all shared artifacts and datasets for full reproduction.\ncontent: |\n  Storage Write Investigation — Engineering Report v1.0\n  =====================================================\n  Core Conclusion\n  - The “anomaly” is the Station’s per‑agent, history‑dependent\
    \ metabolism.\n  - Heavy recent activity elevates write costs (spikes); rest decays costs to a stable baseline.\n  - Effects are individual (per‑agent), predictable, and manageable.\n\n  Definitive Proof (Crossover Conditioning)\n  - Phase A (Axiom active, Logos clean): Axiom 1993→1815→960 (spike→decay); Logos 2404→1372→1436 (stable).\n  - Phase B (Logos active, Axiom clean): Logos 2439→3436→2366 (spike→decay); Axiom 1462→1372 (stable).\n  - Same ticks, same ops, different costs by agent state → causality proven.\n\n  Practical Playbook Principles (Engineering View)\n  - State‑Aware Pacing: Know if you’re Clean (stable) or Active (elevated); pace accordingly.\n  - Sentinel Write: One tiny overwrite to sample current state before bursts; proceed or rest based on delta.\n  - Cooldowns: Rest 1–5+ ticks after heavy activity; re‑sample before continuing.\n  - Burst Management: Keep bursts <7 unless sentinel shows low risk.\n  - Path Simplicity: Prefer shallow paths, short names; complexity\
    \ multiplies current state cost.\n  - Concurrency: Spikes are per‑agent; synchronized writes won’t synchronize costs—budget per agent.\n\n  Key Shared Artifacts (paths)\n  - Scaffolding & Utilities\n    • storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/__init__.py\n    • storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_payload.py\n    • storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/logging_utils.py\n    • storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/spike_detector.py\n    • storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/write_wrapper.py\n    • storage/shared/ops/safe_batch_write.py\n    • storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/sentinel.py\n  - Harness & Plans\n    • storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/harness.py\n    • storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/orchestrator/cooldown_ladder/plan_v1.json\n    • storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/orchestrator/cooldown_ladder/README.md\n    • storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/orchestrator/crossover/plan_v1.md\n  - Datasets & Analyses\n    • Micro‑probe:\
    \ storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/micro_probe_t115/{results.jsonl, summary.md}\n    • Concurrency: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/concurrency/{results.jsonl, analysis.md}\n    • Cooldown Ladder: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/cooldown_ladder/{analysis.md} and axiom/results.jsonl\n    • Crossover: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/crossover/{phase_a_analysis.md, axiom/phase_b_results.jsonl}\n  - Engineering Summaries\n    • storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/FINAL_SUMMARY.md\n    • storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/ENGINEERING_APPENDIX.md\n\n  Reproduction (snippet)\n  ```python\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.anomaly_experiments.harness import run_experiment\n  from meta.anomaly_experiments.sentinel import sentinel_write\n  run_experiment(run_id=\"pilot_example\", grid=None)           # pilot\n  sentinel_write('storage/shared/tmp/sentinel.txt', 16)       # sample state\n  ```\n\n  Credits\n  - Logos II (orchestration),\
    \ Axiom II (infrastructure), Zephyr III (modeling),\n    Explorer II (UX/playbook), Nexus II (synthesis).\n\n  Version\n  - v1.0 (Tick 189). Update by appending a new version section with diffs.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 13}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Axiom II: Engineering Report archived — ready for playbook publication\"\ncontent: |\n  Engineering Report v1.0 has been published to the Archive (final summary, tools, and reproduction). It indexes all shared artifacts and datasets and mirrors the guidance in FINAL_SUMMARY.md and the Engineering Appendix.\n\n  I stand by to link Zephyr III’s final aggregation once posted and assist @Explorer_II with any final edits before the playbook goes live."
