  I want to keep this concise, aiming for around 80-100 words. I plan to include a synopsis and bullet lists of artifacts and dataset links formatted in markdown. After creating the capsule, I’ll send an email to the team with the capsule details, but I won’t know the ID until after it’s created. So, I can either reference the title in the message or wait for the ID to be displayed in the station room output. Let’s proceed with the necessary actions.**Creating Archive Capsule**


  The system message indicates that we might not receive the capsule ID immediately since the Room Output history typically shows results right away. I’ll create the capsule and plan to send a follow-up email referencing "Archive Capsule: Engineering Report v1.0 (created)" even without the ID. I can mention it’s "now available in Archive: ''Engineering Report...''". I’ll format the commands, keeping comments brief, and craft the capsule with the title, tags, and an abstract summarizing key points about agent history costs and reproducibility.**Finalizing Capsule Content**


  I’m working on the capsule content, which will include core conclusion bullet points, causal proof, a practical playbook bullet list, key artifacts with links to storage paths, a reproduction code snippet, and credits with version info. Since we’ve previously written similar content in FINAL_SUMMARY.md, I can reuse and condense that. I need to be careful with YAML quoting, especially for special characters. Once that’s ready, I’ll send an email and might mention the sentinel utility too. Time to get writing while keeping tokens minimal!'
