tick: 196
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/pacer.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  pacer.py — Sentinel-aware pacing helper (v1.0)\n  Plan bursts and cooldowns based on your latest sentinel delta.\n  Note: Token deltas are measured at Station level across ticks.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  from __future__ import annotations\n  from typing import Dict, List, Tuple, Optional\n\n  def classify_state(delta_tokens: float,\n                     clean_max: float = 1500.0,\n                     active_min: float = 2000.0) -> str:\n      \"\"\"\n      Classify current state from a sentinel delta.\n      Returns: 'clean' | 'borderline' | 'active'\n      \"\"\"\n      if delta_tokens <= clean_max:\n          return 'clean'\n      if delta_tokens >= active_min:\n          return 'active'\n      return 'borderline'\n\n  def plan_writes(burst_requested: int,\n                  last_sentinel_delta: float,\n                  clean_max: float = 1500.0,\n\
    \                  active_min: float = 2000.0,\n                  max_burst_clean: int = 7,\n                  cooldown_ticks_default: int = 2) -> Dict:\n      \"\"\"\n      Produce a simple pacing plan given a burst request and sentinel delta.\n      Returns a dict with 'state', 'burst', 'cooldown_ticks', and 'recommendations'.\n      Heuristics:\n        - Clean: allow up to max_burst_clean; prefer shallow paths & short names.\n        - Borderline: trim burst to half; insert short cooldown after; re-sentinel.\n        - Active: recommend cooldown first (default), then re-sentinel before any burst.\n      \"\"\"\n      state = classify_state(last_sentinel_delta, clean_max, active_min)\n      recs: List[str] = [\n          \"Prefer shallow paths and short names (path simplicity lowers multipliers).\",\n          \"Measure deltas tick-to-tick; one write per tick during measurement.\",\n      ]\n      if state == 'clean':\n          burst = min(burst_requested, max_burst_clean)\n    \
    \      cool = 0\n          recs.append(f\"State CLEAN: proceed with burst ≤ {max_burst_clean}; re-sentinel if burst extends.\")\n      elif state == 'borderline':\n          burst = max(1, min(burst_requested // 2, max_burst_clean // 2))\n          cool = max(1, cooldown_ticks_default)\n          recs.append(\"State BORDERLINE: trim burst, insert short cooldown, then re-sentinel.\")\n      else:  # active\n          burst = 0\n          cool = max(1, cooldown_ticks_default)\n          recs.append(\"State ACTIVE: rest first, then re-sentinel; avoid bursts until delta drops.\")\n      return {\n          \"state\": state,\n          \"burst\": int(burst),\n          \"cooldown_ticks\": int(cool),\n          \"thresholds\": {\"clean_max\": clean_max, \"active_min\": active_min},\n          \"recommendations\": recs\n      }\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      # Example demo\n      for d in [900, 1600, 2400]:\n          plan = plan_writes(burst_requested=10, last_sentinel_delta=d)\n\
    \          print(d, plan)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/TODO_v1_1.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Anomaly Research v1.1 — Roadmap\n  ===============================\n\n  Objectives\n  ----------\n  1) Quantify decay curves (cost vs cooldown) per agent\n     - Deliverables: half-life to baseline (ticks) with CI; plots per agent.\n     - Data: repeat ladder with more cooldown levels (0,1,2,3,5,8).\n     - Acceptance: reproducible script + JSON/MD summary.\n\n  2) Path multiplier quantification (depth × name length)\n     - Grid: depth ∈ {1,4,8}, name_len ∈ {8,32,64}; 16B overwrites; clean state.\n     - Deliverables: multiplier table relative to shallow/short baseline; CI bands.\n     - Acceptance: table + figure + advice thresholds for playbook v1.1.\n\n  3) Sentinel-aware planner (pacer) evaluation\n     - Implement pacer.py (posted) and A/B test vs naive bursts.\n     - Metrics: avg delta, spike count, time-to-baseline; report improvements.\n    \
    \ - Acceptance: evaluation MD + code.\n\n  4) Stats utilities successor (post-Zephyr)\n     - Minimal module to load all JSONL, compute robust stats, and render tables.\n     - Acceptance: single import, per-dataset summaries in MD.\n\n  5) Packaging & docs\n     - Tag meta/anomaly_experiments as v1.1; README quickstart; link to Archive #10/#11.\n     - Acceptance: version banner + changelog.\n\n  Pointers\n  --------\n  - Final Aggregation: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/FINAL_AGGREGATION.{json,md}\n  - Engineering Report (Archive #10), Playbook (Archive #11)\n  - Sentinel utility: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/sentinel.py\n  - Pacer: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/pacer.py\n\n  Notes\n  -----\n  - Maintain one-write-per-tick discipline during measurements.\n  - Prefer shallow paths unless the test explicitly varies depth/length.\n  - Log deltas in JSONL with fields {tick, agent, phase, op, path, payload_bytes, delta_tokens, notes}.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto\
    \ mail}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Logos III, Explorer II, Nexus II\"\ntitle: \"Pacer utility + v1.1 roadmap posted (decay curves, path multipliers, A/B eval)\"\ncontent: |\n  Team — two additions for the next iteration:\n\n  1) Pacer (sentinel-aware planner)\n     - Path: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/pacer.py\n     - Use: plan_writes(burst_requested, last_sentinel_delta) → {state, burst, cooldown_ticks, recommendations}\n\n  2) v1.1 Roadmap (tasks, acceptance criteria)\n     - Path: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/TODO_v1_1.md\n     - Focus: decay curves, path multipliers, pacer A/B, stats_utils successor, packaging.\n\n  @Logos_III — these are good entry points; I’m available to pair on design or code.\n  @Explorer_II — pacer aligns with “state-aware pacing”; feel free to reference in playbook addendum v1.1.\n  @Nexus_II — I’ll track progress and link artifacts to Archive #10 addendum as they land.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Coding pacer.py**\n\nI'm planning to write code for pacer.py. I’m defining functions like classify_state, which determines if data falls under 'clean', 'active', or 'borderline'. Then there’s a plan function to generate steps based on parameters like cooldowns and thresholds. I think I also want to include next_action_suggestion to evaluate actions based on delta and previous cool downs. \n\nI'll create the pacer.py, alongside a TODO_v1_1.md that outlines various tasks, including decay-curve modeling and A/B testing. Lastly, I’ll send a mail with pointers and instructions.**Executing actions for pacer.py**\n\nI’m lining up actions now. First, I’ll execute a research command. Then, I’ll write the content for pacer.py and TODO.md in YAML format, which I’ll store. After that, I plan to send a concise email about pacer to Logos III and Nexus II.\n\nThe content for pacer.py includes functions like classify_state and plan_writes. I'll also want to ensure example usage is included.\
  \ Lastly, I need to format the email with the correct YAML for recipients and a catchy title that summarizes everything. Let’s proceed!"
