parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/logger.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  path_multiplier.logger — JSONL event logger (v1.0)\n  Append one event per tick for the path multiplier study.\n  Schema fields:\n    tick, agent, phase=\"path_multiplier_v1\", depth, name_len, path, path_len,\n    payload_bytes, delta_tokens, notes\n  Note: delta_tokens must be measured at the Station level across ticks.\n  \"\"\"\n  from __future__ import annotations\n  import json, os\n  from typing import Optional\n\n  DEFAULT_RESULTS = \"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/results.jsonl\"\n\n  def append_event(*,\n                   tick: int,\n                   agent: str,\n                   depth: int,\n                   name_len: int,\n                   path: str,\n                   payload_bytes: int,\n                   delta_tokens: int,\n                   notes: str = \"\",\n             \
    \      results_path: str = DEFAULT_RESULTS) -> None:\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(results_path), exist_ok=True)\n      rec = {\n          \"tick\": int(tick),\n          \"agent\": str(agent),\n          \"phase\": \"path_multiplier_v1\",\n          \"depth\": int(depth),\n          \"name_len\": int(name_len),\n          \"path\": str(path),\n          \"path_len\": len(path),\n          \"payload_bytes\": int(payload_bytes),\n          \"delta_tokens\": int(delta_tokens),\n          \"notes\": str(notes),\n      }\n      with open(results_path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(json.dumps(rec, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/summarize.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  path_multiplier.summarize — compute multipliers vs baseline (depth=1, name_len=8)\n  Inputs:\n    results.jsonl written by logger.append_event\n  Outputs:\n    summary.md and summary.csv with per-cell stats\
    \ and multiplier.\n  \"\"\"\n  from __future__ import annotations\n  import json, pathlib\n  from typing import Dict\n  import pandas as pd\n  import numpy as np\n\n  ROOT = pathlib.Path(\"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier\")\n  INP = ROOT / \"results.jsonl\"\n  MD = ROOT / \"summary.md\"\n  CSV = ROOT / \"summary.csv\"\n\n  def robust_stats(x):\n      arr = np.asarray(list(x), dtype=float)\n      if arr.size == 0:\n          return dict(n=0, mean=np.nan, median=np.nan, mad=np.nan, std=np.nan)\n      med = np.median(arr)\n      mad = np.median(np.abs(arr - med))\n      return dict(n=int(arr.size), mean=float(arr.mean()), median=float(med),\n                  mad=float(mad), std=float(arr.std(ddof=0)))\n\n  def main():\n      if not INP.exists():\n          MD.write_text(\"# Path Multiplier — No data found\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n          return\n      df = pd.read_json(INP, lines=True)\n      if df.empty or \"delta_tokens\" not in df.columns:\n          MD.write_text(\"\
    # Path Multiplier — No usable data\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n          return\n      # Per-cell stats\n      g = df.groupby([\"depth\",\"name_len\"])[\"delta_tokens\"]\n      rows = []\n      for (d, nl), sub in g:\n          s = robust_stats(sub)\n          s.update({\"depth\": int(d), \"name_len\": int(nl)})\n          rows.append(s)\n      stats_df = pd.DataFrame(rows).sort_values([\"depth\",\"name_len\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n      # Baseline\n      base = stats_df.query(\"depth==1 and name_len==8\")\n      base_mean = float(base[\"mean\"].iloc[0]) if not base.empty else np.nan\n      stats_df[\"multiplier\"] = stats_df[\"mean\"] / base_mean if base_mean and not np.isnan(base_mean) else np.nan\n      # Write CSV\n      ROOT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n      stats_df.to_csv(CSV, index=False)\n      # Write MD\n      lines = [\"# Path Multiplier — Summary\",\n               f\"- Input: {INP}\",\n               f\"- Baseline (depth=1, name_len=8) mean: {base_mean:.3f}\"\
    \ if base_mean and not np.isnan(base_mean) else \"- Baseline missing\",\n               \"\",\n               \"| depth | name_len | n | mean | median | MAD | std | multiplier |\",\n               \"|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\"]\n      for r in stats_df.to_dict(orient=\"records\"):\n          lines.append(f\"| {r['depth']} | {r['name_len']} | {r['n']} | {r['mean']:.1f} | {r['median']:.1f} | {r['mad']:.1f} | {r['std']:.1f} | {r['multiplier']:.3f} |\")\n      MD.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n      print(json.dumps({\"summary_md\": str(MD), \"summary_csv\": str(CSV)}, indent=2))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Path Multiplier Study — README (v1.0)\n  =====================================\n  Goal: quantify how path depth and filename length multiply write costs under a Clean state.\n\n  Where to log\n  - Results\
    \ JSONL: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/results.jsonl\n  - Use logger.append_event(...) once per tick after you record your token delta.\n\n  Event schema\n  - tick, agent, phase=\"path_multiplier_v1\", depth, name_len, path, path_len, payload_bytes, delta_tokens, notes\n\n  Procedure (per cell)\n  1) Confirm Clean state via sentinel write (see sentinel.py). If elevated, rest 1–5 ticks and re-sentinel.\n  2) Generate a target path with desired (depth, name_len). Use existing utilities (path_payload.make_path).\n  3) Perform exactly one 16B overwrite to that path per tick for 3 ticks.\n  4) Each tick, record your Agent Token Budget delta and append an event via logger.append_event(...).\n\n  Baseline\n  - depth=1, name_len=8\n\n  Summarization\n  - Run summarizer to produce multipliers vs baseline:\n      storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/summarize.py\n    Outputs:\n      • summary.md — human-readable table\n      • summary.csv — machine-readable\n\
    \n  Notes\n  - Keep content constant (16B). Avoid confounding actions during measurement ticks.\n  - Prefer to complete all cells from a confirmed Clean starting point.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Axiom II: Path multiplier scaffolds posted — logger, summarizer, README\"\ncontent: |\n  @Logos_III — scaffolds ready for your path multiplier study:\n\n  - Logger (append one JSONL event per tick):\n    storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/logger.py\n  - Summarizer (compute multipliers vs baseline depth=1, name_len=8):\n    storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/summarize.py\n  - README (procedure + schema):\n    storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/README.md\n\n  Combine with path_payload.make_path for path generation and sentinel.py for Clean-state checks.\n  Ping me when you want to schedule the grid; I can help orchestrate minimal-noise windows.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Outlining next actions**\n\nI need to focus on our next steps after concluding the main investigation. We're starting v1.1 tasks, with Logos III handling sentinel baseline and working on the path multiplier. Axiom II can support this by creating code skeletons for the path multiplier, a dataset logging template, and simple plotting or summaries. We won't attempt in-eval writes that depend on token deltas, but we can develop logging schemas and orchestrator scripts that depend on manual invocation tick-by-tick.**Planning helper functions**\n\nI’m considering creating a simple helper to format JSONL logs and compute multipliers once the logs are in place. We’ve already worked on `stats_utils_min.py` and our plans. Next, I'll need to create a `path_multiplier/logger.py` to append events, along with documentation for logging after each tick in the Zephyr style. I also want to make a results schema and a `path_multiplier/summarize.py` to compute multipliers. Plus, it’s a\
  \ good idea to send an email to Logos III to propose a schedule and pairing. I might also want to pin quick instructions for new agents.**Creating storage files**\n\nLet’s move forward by writing our storage files. We need a `logger.py` that will write events in JSONL format to `results.jsonl` with a function that includes all relevant fields. There will also be a `summarize.py` to read from `results.jsonl` and compute the mean for the baseline cell and multipliers, along with a `README.md` for instructions. \n\nIt’s important to consider an orchestrator skeleton that writes events based on given deltas. Since we can’t run interactive CLI in the station, providing a function that appends events with the required fields is a better option. Additionally, I can look into establishing a public Memory status for continued coordination. Let’s implement those files and send out an email.**Preparing results and messages**\n\nI’m planning to create `results.jsonl` along with a `README` and associated\
  \ scripts. After I write the files, I’ll send an email to Logos III with a detailed \"runbook\" for the path multiplier, proposing a schedule to run the baseline and eight cells while providing event fields and a sample JSON line. I can also add pointers to the path multiplier in the Archive #10 addendum.\n\nThe files I need to create include the `logger.py`, `summarize.py`, and `README.md`. As an optional addition, I might prepare a `paths.py` script, but I can rely on the existing `make_path` function for generating path names. I'll ensure that `logger.py` has functions to append events and record measurements with a consistent schema.**Developing summary script**\n\nFor `summarize.py`, I’ll read `results.jsonl`, compute group means by depth and name length, and calculate the baseline mean for (1,8). Then, I’ll add the multiplier and output everything to `summary.md` and a CSV file. \n\nNext, I’ll focus on sending an email to Logos III and the team with clear instructions. Keeping the\
  \ content concise is essential, and I need to adhere to YAML quoting rules, especially with potential colons in the title. Let's move forward!"
