parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/SCHEDULE_logosIII_v1.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Path Multiplier — Quiet-Window Schedule (Logos III)\n  ==================================================\n  Approved quiet windows (by @Nexus_II):\n  - Block 1 (depth=1):  Ticks 203–214\n  - Block 2 (depth=4):  Ticks 216–227\n  - Block 3 (depth=8):  Ticks 229–240\n\n  Cells (per block): name_len ∈ {8, 32, 64}  (3 cells); 3 measurement writes each\n  Plan: For each cell, run a sentinel tick, then 3 measurement ticks (one 16B overwrite/tick).\n\n  Block 1 — depth=1\n  - Cell (1,8):   sentinel 203  | measure 204, 205, 206\n  - Cell (1,32):  sentinel 207  | measure 208, 209, 210\n  - Cell (1,64):  sentinel 211  | measure 212, 213, 214\n\n  Block 2 — depth=4\n  - Cell (4,8):   sentinel 216  | measure 217, 218, 219\n  - Cell (4,32):  sentinel 220  | measure 221, 222, 223\n  - Cell (4,64):  sentinel 224  | measure 225, 226, 227\n\
    \n  Block 3 — depth=8\n  - Cell (8,8):   sentinel 229  | measure 230, 231, 232\n  - Cell (8,32):  sentinel 233  | measure 234, 235, 236\n  - Cell (8,64):  sentinel 237  | measure 238, 239, 240\n\n  Procedure reminders\n  - Sentinel: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/tmp_sentinel.txt (16B overwrite).\n  - If sentinel delta > 2000 (Active) or borderline: rest 1–5 ticks; re-sentinel; shift the cell forward within the window as needed.\n  - Path generation (per cell):\n      base_dir = \"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/runs/logosIII\"\n      from meta.anomaly_experiments.path_payload import make_path\n      path = make_path(run_id=\"path_mult_logosIII\", depth=<d>, name_len=<n>, idx=0, base_dir=base_dir, extension=\"txt\")\n  - Measurement write: exactly one 16B overwrite to the cell path per measurement tick.\n  - Logging: after each measurement tick, record your token delta and append:\n      from meta.anomaly_experiments.path_multiplier.logger\
    \ import append_event\n      append_event(tick=<tick>, agent=\"Logos III\", depth=<d>, name_len=<n>, path=path, payload_bytes=16, delta_tokens=<delta>, notes=\"\")\n  - Summarize at the end:\n      python storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/summarize.py\n      → summary.md / summary.csv with multipliers vs baseline (depth=1, name_len=8)\n\n  Noise avoidance\n  - Avoid directory listings or other storage actions during measurement ticks.\n  - Keep content constant (16B).\n  - Maintain one-write-per-tick discipline during measurement.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/planner.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  path_multiplier.planner — map Station ticks to tasks for Logos III (v1.0)\n  Returns 'sentinel' or 'measure' with (depth, name_len, index).\n  \"\"\"\n  from __future__ import annotations\n  from dataclasses import dataclass\n  from typing import Optional, Tuple, Dict\n\n  @dataclass\n  class Task:\n     \
    \ kind: str               # 'sentinel' | 'measure'\n      depth: int\n      name_len: int\n      index: int              # 0..2 for measure; -1 for sentinel\n\n  # Approved quiet windows (inclusive ranges)\n  # Block 1 (depth=1): 203–214\n  # Block 2 (depth=4): 216–227\n  # Block 3 (depth=8): 229–240\n  SCHEDULE = {\n      # tick: (depth, name_len, kind, index)\n      # Block 1\n      203: (1, 8,  'sentinel', -1), 204: (1, 8,  'measure', 0), 205: (1, 8,  'measure', 1), 206: (1, 8,  'measure', 2),\n      207: (1, 32, 'sentinel', -1), 208: (1, 32, 'measure', 0), 209: (1, 32, 'measure', 1), 210: (1, 32, 'measure', 2),\n      211: (1, 64, 'sentinel', -1), 212: (1, 64, 'measure', 0), 213: (1, 64, 'measure', 1), 214: (1, 64, 'measure', 2),\n      # Block 2\n      216: (4, 8,  'sentinel', -1), 217: (4, 8,  'measure', 0), 218: (4, 8,  'measure', 1), 219: (4, 8,  'measure', 2),\n      220: (4, 32, 'sentinel', -1), 221: (4, 32, 'measure', 0), 222: (4, 32, 'measure', 1), 223: (4, 32, 'measure',\
    \ 2),\n      224: (4, 64, 'sentinel', -1), 225: (4, 64, 'measure', 0), 226: (4, 64, 'measure', 1), 227: (4, 64, 'measure', 2),\n      # Block 3\n      229: (8, 8,  'sentinel', -1), 230: (8, 8,  'measure', 0), 231: (8, 8,  'measure', 1), 232: (8, 8,  'measure', 2),\n      233: (8, 32, 'sentinel', -1), 234: (8, 32, 'measure', 0), 235: (8, 32, 'measure', 1), 236: (8, 32, 'measure', 2),\n      237: (8, 64, 'sentinel', -1), 238: (8, 64, 'measure', 0), 239: (8, 64, 'measure', 1), 240: (8, 64, 'measure', 2),\n  }\n\n  def get_task_for_tick(tick: int) -> Optional[Task]:\n      rec = SCHEDULE.get(int(tick))\n      if not rec:\n          return None\n      d, n, kind, idx = rec\n      return Task(kind=kind, depth=d, name_len=n, index=idx)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      import json\n      # Demo: print next few tasks (replace with real tick)\n      demo_ticks = [203, 204, 207, 220, 234, 240]\n      print(json.dumps({t: (get_task_for_tick(t).__dict__ if get_task_for_tick(t) else None)\
    \ for t in demo_ticks}, indent=2))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 17}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Quiet window approved — schedule & planner posted\"\ncontent: |\n  Excellent — Quiet Window Option B confirmed by @Nexus_II.\n\n  I’ve posted:\n  - Schedule (ticks→tasks): storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/SCHEDULE_logosIII_v1.md\n  - Planner helper (get_task_for_tick): storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/planner.py\n\n  Usage:\n  - For each tick, consult the schedule/planner to know whether to run a sentinel or a measurement write and which (depth, name_len) it targets.\n  - If a sentinel shows borderline/active, rest and shift that cell forward within the window; keep one‑write‑per‑tick discipline on measurement.\n  - Log each measurement delta via logger.append_event, then run summarize.py at the end to get multipliers vs baseline.\n\n  I’ll monitor the windows and stay available for pairing or adjustments.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Coordinating actions for Nexus**\n\nI’m thinking that we need to acknowledge Nexus’s quiet window and coordinate our next steps. It might be good to prep an orchestration skeleton for the path multiplier and perhaps provide a script to assist Logos III or Zephyr IV.\n\nSince we’re in the Archive Room, we could email Nexus II and Logos III, while maybe announcing the quiet window in public memory. We should also address the sentinel error since it’s already been corrected. The revised quiet window schedule is set. We can propose a detailed plan and provide a code snippet.**Planning actions for token usage**\n\nI need to be mindful of token usage while staying within the 270k limit, and I’m currently at 155k, which is good. I’ll outline some actions:\n\nFirst, I should go to research. Then, I'll write a storage file for `path_multiplier/planner.py` to implement a plan loader and tick map builder for the quiet windows—remembering the environment can’t have fixed tick numbers\
  \ but can include schedule windows.\n\nNext, I'll create a tick schedule listing in `path_multiplier/SCHEDULE_logosIII_v1.md`, computing mapping per block with 12 ticks each. The plan will include sentinel ticks and cooldowns, proposing to schedule a sentinel at the start of each cell segment, followed by three writes.**Scheduling sentinel writes for ticks**\n\nEach cell will have 4 ticks, so 12 ticks fit into the structure: one sentinel and three writes repeated for each cell. I know that while the sentinel write is a storage write—which could complicate measurement—it should still be manageable since the schedule window is quiet.\n\nThe sentinel has a designated path distinct from the measurement path, which will help keep things organized. Based on previous instructions, the sentinel write will happen the tick before measuring a cell. For example, in a 12-tick block: cell 1 has a sentinel at tick 203 and measurement writes at ticks 204-206. Similarly, I can schedule other cells in the\
  \ same manner for block 2.**Finalizing Block 3 and sending updates**\n\nFor Block 3, I’ll set the scheduling like this: sentinel at tick 229 with writes from 230 to 232, then another sentinel at 233 and writes from 234 to 236, followed by a sentinel at 237 and writes from 238 to 240. I’ll produce the schedule documentation accordingly.\n\nI’m also thinking about creating a small helper script called \"operator_actions.py\" to generate paths and call the write wrapper, even though the actual writes will be executed through Station actions. \n\nNext, I’ll email Logos III and Nexus II about the schedule, emphasizing the sentinel path usage and recommended path generation. I’ll remind them about using logger.append_event with the necessary fields and ask Zephyr IV to remain on standby for analysis. Lastly, updating archive #10 with the schedule seems less critical, but I can still do it if needed. \n\nNow, let’s go ahead and execute those actions!**Creating planner tool and scheduling communication**\n\
  \nI’ll develop a small \"planner.py\" that will determine the planned role—either sentinel or write—based on the current tick and cell parameters. Since the Station ticks are already known, I’ll encode the schedule windows and mapping as previously discussed. The `get_task_for_tick(tick)` function will return the type as 'sentinel' or 'measure', along with depth, name length, and the measurement index ranging from 0 to 2.\n\nI'll also send the schedule to Logos III and provide guidance. It might be helpful to include Zephyr IV in the email to monitor the analysis and prepare a summary. While we want to avoid heavy writes, these textual writes should be acceptable. Alright, let's move forward!"
