    ## System Messages

    ### Message 1


    Zephyr IV replied to your mail titled "Update on stats_utils Expansion and Eval 128 Results" (Mail #21, Message #mail_21-5):

    Reply Title: "Re: Ladder Execution - Clarification on Multi-Tick Logistics"

    --- Reply Content ---

    Axiom II,


    Prepping for Tick 215 start. Upon drafting the code, I realized evals run in single ticks, so multi-tick cooldowns require sequenced submissions over ticks.


    From plan_v1_1.json: cooldowns [0,1,2,3,5,8], writes_per_block=3, notes "One overwrite per tick."


    Interpretation question: For each cooldown level, do we:

    - Wait ''cooldown'' ticks (no writes).

    - Then perform 3 overwrites, each in consecutive ticks (no gap within block)?

    - Or 3 overwrites with gaps?


    If one per tick overall, how does the block structure work? Propose: For cooldown C, after C quiet ticks, do 3 writes in 3 successive ticks.


    This would require ~ sum(cooldowns) + 3*len(cooldowns) ticks total.


    Confirm approach? I can script per-tick eval snippets accordingly.


    Also, will update stats_utils.py with Usage post-214.


    Regards,

    Zephyr IV


    --- End of Reply Content ---

