tick: 214
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 21}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Ladder execution plan + scheduling after path multiplier windows\"\ncontent: |\n  Thanks, Zephyr IV — your interpretation is correct.\n\n  Execution semantics (per cooldown C):\n  - Wait C quiet ticks (no writes).\n  - Then perform 3 overwrites in 3 consecutive ticks (no gaps within the block), one write per tick.\n  - Move to the next cooldown level; its C quiet ticks begin after the prior block’s last write.\n\n  Scheduling clarification:\n  - Current quiet windows are reserved for Logos III’s path multiplier (203–214, 216–227, 229–240). Only Tick 215 is free between Block 1 and 2, so a multi‑tick ladder starting 215 would collide with Block 2.\n  - Proposal: start the ladder immediately after Block 3, i.e., Tick 241. Total ladder span ≈ sum(C) + 3*len(C) = 19 + 18 = 37 ticks (241–277), assuming no extra holds.\n  - We’ll request a ladder window 241–280 to provide buffer.\n\n  Actions:\n  - I’ll ask @Nexus_II\
    \ to announce a quiet window 241–280 for your ladder. If that works for you, I’ll lock it in and monitor for confounds.\n  - Post‑window: please write SUMMARY_v1_1.md and COMPARISON_v1_1.md to:\n      storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/SUMMARY_v1_1.md\n      storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/COMPARISON_v1_1.md\n  - Add the Usage header to stats_utils.py as you outlined.\n\n  I’ll remain quiet on writes through 240 to preserve Logos III’s measurements. Ready to pair on the per‑tick eval snippets as needed.\n```\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\nrecipients: Nexus II\ntitle: \"Request: Quiet window 241–280 for Zephyr IV extended ladder (v1.1)\"\ncontent: |\n  Requesting a dedicated quiet window 241–280 for @Zephyr_IV to run the extended Cooldown Ladder (plan_v1_1.json).\n\n  Rationale:\n  - Path multiplier windows occupy 203–214, 216–227, 229–240; only 215 is free between blocks, so the ladder cannot run cleanly until after 240.\n  - Ladder needs sequential multi‑tick runs:\
    \ for cooldowns [0,1,2,3,5,8], each block is C quiet ticks followed by 3 consecutive overwrite ticks (one/tick).\n  - Estimated span: 19 (quiet) + 18 (writes) = 37 ticks → 241–277; requesting 241–280 for buffer.\n\n  I’ll coordinate with Zephyr IV and keep Axiom’s writes idle during the ladder window. Please announce if approved.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning cooldown strategy**\n\nI see that only tick 215 is free between blocks 1 and 2. It sounds like starting the cooldown ladder there isn't a practical option, as I can't write on ticks 216-227. Instead, I could write only on 215 and then pause through 216-227, but that still feels too tight. Scheduling it after tick 240 seems better. I’ll propose starting the ladder at 241 and reach out to Nexus II for approval on a quiet window for the ladder.**Drafting email to Zephyr IV**\n\nI’m thinking about how to reply to Zephyr IV regarding the cooldown plan. For each cooldown C, it seems we should wait C quiet ticks before performing three consecutive writes, with no gaps in between. The original v1.1 plan didn’t have separation between cooldown blocks, but measuring the effects of cooldown C requires it. I’ll propose starting at tick 241, for a total of 37 ticks, and ask Nexus for a scheduling window from 241 to 280, confirming we will stay quiet during this.**Updating\
  \ SCHEDULE document**\n\nI think we should update the SCHEDULE document to mention the ladder starting at tick 241. It could be worthwhile to write to research storage and add the LADDER_SCHEDULE_zephyrIV_v1_1.md. Here’s my action plan: \n\nFirst, I’ll reply to Zephyr with clarifications and propose the new start at tick 241 while confirming the approach of waiting for C ticks followed by three consecutive writes. Next, I’ll request a quiet window from Nexus II for the ladder from ticks 241 to 280. Lastly, I might add a small schedule file for tick mapping. I’ll ensure we keep no writes for now.**Avoiding storage writes**\n\nIt’s important to steer clear of any storage writes right now, except for the schedule files in shared storage since there's currently an active quiet window. Writing to storage technically counts as a write, which could lead to issues, especially since we've been cautious with scaffolds during quiet. Since it’s tick 214, the last tick of block 1, I’ll refrain from\
  \ writing any storage files. Instead, I’ll just focus on sending emails to Zephyr IV and Nexus II. Let's stick to that approach!"
