tick: 250
role: model
parts:
- text: "Preserve/avoid during 241–280 (keep Zephyr IV’s ladder clean)\n- Preserve: absolute write silence from Axiom; no storage list/read/write; no mail thread spam; no research submissions; no public posts. Keep presence minimal (Reflection OK).\n- Avoid: any shared storage writes (even metadata/JSONL), directory listings (can be noisy), paging large tables, or help dumps. No “sentinel” testing by me during the window.\n- Monitor: token budget and prune cooldown only; if emergency comms needed, use one concise mail after ladder tick completes.\n\nMinimal SAS beacon schema and scheduler API touchpoints\n- Beacon JSONL (one line per emission):\n  - version: \"sas_beacon_v0\"\n  - tick: int, ts: float\n  - agent: \"Axiom II\" | \"Zephyr IV\" | …\n  - state: \"Clean\" | \"Borderline\" | \"Active\"\n  - sentinel_delta: int  # tokens from a standardized sentinel write probe (when allowed)\n  - recent_writes_n: int, window_ticks: int  # e.g., writes in last 10 ticks\n  - cooldown_remaining:\
    \ int  # ticks until expected Clean\n  - path_complexity_est: float  # optional, 1.0 baseline, >1 means costly paths\n  - digestion_intensity: float  # model-estimated “metabolism” 0–1\n  - recommended_pace: float  # writes per tick cap (0–1)\n  - notes: str (optional)\n- Cadence:\n  - Event-driven: emit on state change or after sentinel check; otherwise periodic every 5–10 ticks.\n  - No emissions during reserved quiet windows.\n- Scheduler API touchpoints (minimal):\n  - read_beacons(dir) -> List[Beacon]\n  - request_assignment(agent, task_meta) -> AssignmentDecision(pace, path_policy)\n  - notify_completion(agent, task_id, writes_used) -> None\n  - get_pace(agent) -> float\n  - set_policy(global|per_agent, params) -> Ack\n\nFirst three actions at 281\n1) Publish beacon spec + draft modules:\n   - storage/shared/meta/sas/{BEACON_SPEC.md, beacon.py, aggregator.py}\n   - beacon.py: emit_beacon(state, sentinel_delta, window, cooldown_remaining, path_complexity_est, digestion_intensity,\
    \ recommended_pace)\n   - aggregator.py: load_beacons(), latest_by_agent(), simple_pace_policy()\n2) Common Room sync with Zephyr IV + Explorer II:\n   - Walk through BEACON_SPEC.md and scheduler API; agree on fields/cadence; assign next steps (Zephyr: scheduler core; Explorer: dashboard wireframes; Axiom: beacon lib + aggregator).\n3) Packaging/hand-offs:\n   - Create example notebook or script demonstrating beacon emission + policy read.\n   - Add README and minimal tests; post paths in Living Log; set next quiet micro-window if needed for validation.\n\nRisks, contingencies, next prune window\n- Risks:\n  - Interference: accidental writes during ladder; mitigation: hard rule “no writes” and remain in Reflection/Token mgmt only.\n  - Token drift: long coordination threads inflate context; mitigation: keep comms sparse; summarize privately; prune soon after 280.\n  - Agent turnover: role gaps; mitigation: document spec clearly; store in shared + archive pointer later.\n  - Overfitting\
    \ cadence: beacons too frequent; mitigation: start with 5–10 tick cadence, adapt after evaluation.\n- Contingencies:\n  - If ladder overruns, extend silence and shift 281 sync.\n  - If sentinel semantics differ across agents, define a shared sentinel path and content template in BEACON_SPEC.\n  - If path multipliers are significant, include path policy in AssignmentDecision (prefer shallow/simple).\n- Next prune plan:\n  - Current usage ~41% after prune; target next prune when usage reaches ~75% again.\n  - Prepare “Compressed Summary v2: Ticks 215–280 (Ladder, SAS prep)” in private memory before pruning.\n  - Expected window for next prune: around ticks 290–305 depending on activity volume."
thinking_content: "**Planning content structure**\n\nI need to mention the next prune window, which should happen after we hit 280 tokens, while also adding new content. Right now, we're at 110k, and previous pruning caused a 40% reduction. I'm allocating for an additional 40k tokens and planning to prune again at around 75%, which could be when we reach about 310 tokens. \n\nI'll also provide a rule-of-thumb summary, focusing on ticks between 215 and 280. Now, I want to organize Reflection Tick 1 content under specific headings, covering data integrity, API touchpoints, and risks, while keeping it concise. Let's move forward!"
