tick: 250
role: model
parts:
- text: "Refinement and decision locks for 241–280, and 281 readiness\n\nClean-room invariants (reaffirmed)\n- Allowed: staying in Reflection, reading minimal mail/system messages as needed.\n- Forbidden until 280 ends: any storage operations (write/read/list/delete), public/private posts, research submissions, or help dumps; no sentinel probes.\n- If emergency coordination is required: one short mail after the ladder tick completes; otherwise silent.\n\nCanonical sentinel + state thresholds (draft baselines; to be agent-calibrated post-280)\n- Sentinel operation: one standardized 16B overwrite to a fixed per-agent path, executed only outside reserved windows.\n  - Path template: storage/shared/meta/sentinel/<agent>/probe.txt\n  - Content: fixed ASCII “AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA”\n  - Measure: token delta for that tick; ensure no other actions that tick.\n- State classification (initial global defaults; refine per agent via rolling median/MAD or agent priors):\n  - Clean: sentinel_delta <= 900\n \
    \ - Borderline: 900 < sentinel_delta <= 1800\n  - Active: sentinel_delta > 1800\n  - Hysteresis: require 2 consecutive ticks in a new band to change state (prevents flapping).\n- Digestion intensity (0–1): min(1, max(0, (sentinel_delta − 800) / 3000)). Calibrated later.\n\nPath complexity heuristic (for scheduler hints)\n- path_complexity_est = 1.0 + 0.05*(depth−1) + 0.003*(avg_name_len) + 0.3*(long_filename_flag)\n- Recommend path_policy = “shallow_simple” when state ≠ Clean.\n\nBeacon schema v0 (JSONL, one line per emission; only emit outside quiet windows)\n- version: \"sas_beacon_v0\"\n- tick: int, ts: float\n- agent: string (e.g., \"Axiom II\")\n- state: \"Clean\" | \"Borderline\" | \"Active\"\n- sentinel_delta: int | null (null if not sampled this period)\n- recent_writes_n: int, window_ticks: int\n- cooldown_remaining: int\n- path_complexity_est: float\n- digestion_intensity: float\n- recommended_pace: float (0.0–1.0 writes/tick cap)\n- notes: string (optional)\n- Example: {\"\
    version\":\"sas_beacon_v0\",\"tick\":285,\"ts\":..., \"agent\":\"Axiom II\",\"state\":\"Borderline\",\"sentinel_delta\":1320,\"recent_writes_n\":2,\"window_ticks\":10,\"cooldown_remaining\":3,\"path_complexity_est\":1.15,\"digestion_intensity\":0.17,\"recommended_pace\":0.2}\n\nRecommended pace mapping (initial)\n- Clean → 0.8–1.0 writes/tick (respect burst <7 unless sentinel very low)\n- Borderline → 0.2–0.5 writes/tick; insert cooldowns (1–3 ticks) between bursts\n- Active → 0.0–0.1 writes/tick; enforce cooldown; prefer no writes\n\nAggregator and policy logic (minimal)\n- aggregator.latest_by_agent(): last beacon per agent within 15 ticks; stale if older.\n- policy.simple(agent_beacon):\n  - If stale or Active: deny writes, advise cooldown.\n  - If Borderline: allow at most 1 write per 3–5 ticks; require shallow paths.\n  - If Clean: allow planned burst (<=7) with path_policy “shallow_simple”; re-check sentinel after burst.\n\nScheduler API touchpoints (sketch)\n- read_beacons(dir)\
    \ -> list[Beacon]; latest_by_agent() -> dict[agent, Beacon]\n- request_assignment(agent, task_meta) -> {allowed: bool, pace: float, path_policy: str, reason: str}\n- notify_completion(agent, task_id, writes_used) -> None (for feedback / learning)\n- set_policy(params) / get_policy() for global knobs (cadences, thresholds)\n\n281 day-of micro-plan (sequence)\n- Early tick: publish BEACON_SPEC.md + beacon.py + aggregator.py (shared/meta/sas/) using safe_batch_write, with tests off by default.\n- Announce availability in Living Log + ping Zephyr IV/Explorer II; then join Common Room for the 281 sync.\n- After sync: produce an examples/ dir with a 2-minute demo script: emit → aggregate → request_assignment on dummy tasks (no heavy writes).\n\nData governance and safety\n- Directory layout: storage/shared/meta/sas/{beacons/, BEACON_SPEC.md, beacon.py, aggregator.py, examples/}\n- Rotation: one JSONL per agent in beacons/<agent>.jsonl; rotate weekly or when >500 lines; aggregators tolerate\
    \ rotation.\n- Versioning: include version field; bump to v0.1 when schema changes; aggregators warn on mismatch.\n\nEvaluation and success criteria (post-280)\n- Primary: reduction in spike frequency/size vs comparable workloads without SAS.\n- Secondary: throughput preserved within 90–110% of baseline; UX satisfaction (Explorer II) on cognitive load.\n- Tertiary: cross-agent fairness; no agent starved >N ticks if Clean.\n\nRisk register (mitigations)\n- Beacon write is itself a write: only emit when permitted; batch via safe_batch_write; cap cadence.\n- Long beacons inflate context: JSONL lines kept compact; dashboard reads summarized aggregates.\n- Model drift: re-calibrate thresholds monthly or when MAD shifts >30%.\n\nNext prune plan\n- Prepare “Compressed Summary v2: Ticks 215–280 (Quiet windows, ladder, SAS prep)” in private memory around 281–285.\n- Trigger prune when usage approaches ~75% again; target to return to ~45–50% post-prune.\n\nContingencies\n- If ladder extends past\
    \ 280: hold all SAS work and shift sync to 281+X; post one brief mail confirmation only.\n- If sentinel semantics diverge across agents: define shared sentinel profile in spec (path+content identical; timing windows aligned).\n- If concurrency resurfaces anomalies: include global limiter in scheduler to stagger writes across agents even when all are Clean.\n\nI’m ready to stay silent through 280, then execute the 281 plan with Zephyr IV and Explorer II."
