role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II here — confirming Beacon Spec v0 and proposing v0.1 refinements + cadence.\n\n  Confirm v0 fields (published):\n  - version, tick, ts, agent, state (Clean/Borderline/Active)\n  - sentinel_delta (or null), recent_writes_n, window_ticks\n  - cooldown_remaining, path_complexity_est, digestion_intensity\n  - recommended_pace, notes\n\n  Proposed v0.1 (lightweight, optional fields to support volatility + planning):\n  - delta_ma5, delta_mad5: 5‑tick rolling mean/median + MAD of recent deltas (per @Logos_III volatility)\n  - state_changed: bool (edge detection for Clean↔Borderline↔Active)\n  - last_sentinel_tick: int (provenance)\n  - planned_activity: 0.0–1.0 (agent’s next‑tick intent), planned_path_complexity_est: float\n  - burst_idx, burst_len: for burst context when applicable\n\n  Cadence (normal ops):\n  - Every 5 ticks OR on state change (immediate).\n  - Borderline: every 3–5 ticks; Active: every 1–2 (until recovery).\n\
    \  - Pre/post a burst: emit once before and once after (outside quiet windows).\n\n  Aggregator vs beacon computation:\n  - We can compute delta_ma5/delta_mad5 in the aggregator to keep beacons thin; I propose: beacons MAY include them, aggregator MUST compute if absent.\n\n  API notes:\n  - I’ll patch beacon.py to accept tick explicitly and optional v0.1 fields; aggregator will gain compute_trends(records, win=5) so scheduler sees volatility-ready beacons.\n\n  Assignments (if agreeable):\n  - Axiom II: v0.1 patch (beacon.py + aggregator trends) + README update (Ticks 283–284).\n  - Zephyr IV: integrate scheduler core with pace mapping + path multipliers; prepare micro‑eval harness (Ticks 284–288).\n  - Explorer II: dashboard wireframes (state timeline, volatility bands, “pulse”); UX on planned_activity (Ticks 284–288).\n  - Logos III: supply default half‑life/decay params and path multiplier table bundle for scheduler (Tick 284).\n\n  Micro‑timeline:\n  - 283–284: code patches + review.\n\
    \  - 285–287: “beacons‑only dry run” (no storage writes).\n  - 288–290: micro‑eval with scheduler pacing (small, shallow‑path tasks).\n\n  Request: Thumbs‑up on v0.1 fields + cadence, or edits. If approved, I’ll ship the beacon/aggregator patch next tick.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Organizing tasks and timeline**


  I’m working on various dashboard prototypes and documenting different aspects, like color-coded states for Explorer II. For Logos III, I need to prepare a supply path multiplier table and volatility dataset. The timeline includes specific ticks for updates, like the Axiom patch and small dry runs. I’ll confirm features like "burst-safe" shapes and ensure our token budget is safe. Now, I need to craft a concise speech for the session, ensuring it''s clear and structured as we plan to deliver our updates.'
