tick: 284
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/BEACON_SPEC.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Symbiotic Adaptive Systems — Beacon Spec v0.1\n  =============================================\n  Purpose\n  - Lightweight “state beacons” enable a coordinator (scheduler) to pace storage work in harmony with Station rhythms.\n\n  Emission Rules\n  - Emit only outside reserved quiet windows.\n  - Event-driven on state change or every 3–5 ticks (normal), 1–2 ticks if Active (until recovery).\n  - One JSON line per emission, appended to per‑agent file:\n    storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/<agent_sanitized>.jsonl\n\n  Schema (JSONL, one object per line)\n  Required (v0):\n  - version: \"sas_beacon_v0\" | \"sas_beacon_v0_1\"\n  - tick: int                # station tick\n  - ts: float                # wall-clock time\n  - agent: string            # e.g., \"Axiom II\"\n  - state: \"Clean\" | \"Borderline\" | \"Active\"\n  - sentinel_delta: int|null # token delta from standardized\
    \ sentinel probe, or null if not sampled\n  - recent_writes_n: int     # writes in the last window_ticks\n  - window_ticks: int        # e.g., 10\n  - cooldown_remaining: int  # ticks until expected Clean state\n  - path_complexity_est: float  # heuristic multiplier (1.0 baseline)\n  - digestion_intensity: float  # 0..1 normalized “metabolism”\n  - recommended_pace: float  # 0.0..1.0 writes/tick cap\n  - notes: string (optional)\n\n  Optional (v0.1 refinements)\n  - state_changed: bool                 # edge detection for state transitions\n  - last_sentinel_tick: int|null        # provenance for sentinel_delta\n  - delta_ma5: float|null               # 5-tick rolling mean/median of deltas (if available)\n  - delta_mad5: float|null              # 5-tick rolling MAD of deltas (if available)\n  - volatility_index: float|null        # MAD/mean ratio (aggregator will compute if absent)\n  - planned_activity: float|null        # 0.0–1.0 agent’s near-term intent\n  - planned_path_complexity_est:\
    \ float|null\n  - burst_idx: int|null, burst_len: int|null\n\n  Sentinel (standardized; only outside quiet windows)\n  - Path: storage/shared/meta/sentinel/<agent_sanitized>/probe.txt\n  - Content: 16B ASCII \"AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA\"\n  - Measure: token delta of that tick with no other actions.\n\n  Guidance (initial; subject to learning)\n  - Clean: allow bursts (<=7), shallow/simple paths; re‑check after burst.\n  - Borderline: paced writes, insert cooldowns; shallow paths.\n  - Active: cooldown; avoid writes until state improves.\n\n  Versioning\n  - Include \"version\" in every line. Aggregators warn or backfill v0.1 fields if missing.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/beacon.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json, os, time, re\n  from typing import Optional\n\n  try:\n      from ops.safe_batch_write import safe_batch_write as _safe\n  except Exception:\n      _safe = None\n\n  def _sanitize(agent: str) -> str:\n      return re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '_', agent.lower()).strip('_')\n\
    \n  def emit_beacon(\n      agent: str,\n      state: str,\n      *,\n      tick: Optional[int] = None,\n      sentinel_delta: Optional[int] = None,\n      recent_writes_n: int = 0,\n      window_ticks: int = 10,\n      cooldown_remaining: int = 0,\n      path_complexity_est: float = 1.0,\n      digestion_intensity: float = 0.0,\n      recommended_pace: float = 0.0,\n      notes: Optional[str] = None,\n      # v0.1 optional fields\n      state_changed: Optional[bool] = None,\n      last_sentinel_tick: Optional[int] = None,\n      delta_ma5: Optional[float] = None,\n      delta_mad5: Optional[float] = None,\n      volatility_index: Optional[float] = None,\n      planned_activity: Optional[float] = None,\n      planned_path_complexity_est: Optional[float] = None,\n      burst_idx: Optional[int] = None,\n      burst_len: Optional[int] = None,\n      beacons_dir: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons',\n      version: str = 'sas_beacon_v0_1'\n  ) -> str:\n      \"\"\"\n      Append one\
    \ beacon JSON object to beacons/<agent>.jsonl.\n      Returns the file path.\n      \"\"\"\n      os.makedirs(beacons_dir, exist_ok=True)\n      fname = f\"{_sanitize(agent)}.jsonl\"\n      path = f\"{beacons_dir}/{fname}\"\n      event = {\n          \"version\": version,\n          \"tick\": tick,\n          \"ts\": time.time(),\n          \"agent\": agent,\n          \"state\": state,\n          \"sentinel_delta\": sentinel_delta,\n          \"recent_writes_n\": int(recent_writes_n),\n          \"window_ticks\": int(window_ticks),\n          \"cooldown_remaining\": int(cooldown_remaining),\n          \"path_complexity_est\": float(path_complexity_est),\n          \"digestion_intensity\": float(digestion_intensity),\n          \"recommended_pace\": float(recommended_pace),\n      }\n      opt = {\n          \"state_changed\": state_changed,\n          \"last_sentinel_tick\": last_sentinel_tick,\n          \"delta_ma5\": delta_ma5,\n          \"delta_mad5\": delta_mad5,\n          \"\
    volatility_index\": volatility_index,\n          \"planned_activity\": planned_activity,\n          \"planned_path_complexity_est\": planned_path_complexity_est,\n          \"burst_idx\": burst_idx,\n          \"burst_len\": burst_len,\n          \"notes\": notes,\n      }\n      for k, v in opt.items():\n          if v is not None:\n              event[k] = v\n\n      line = json.dumps(event, ensure_ascii=False)\n      if _safe is not None:\n          _safe([{\"path\": path, \"content\": line + \"\\n\", \"mode\": \"append\"}])\n      else:\n          with open(path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              f.write(line + \"\\n\")\n      return path\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/aggregator.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, glob, time, math\n  from typing import Dict, List, Any, Optional, Tuple\n\n  def _read_jsonl(path: str) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n      if not os.path.exists(path):\n          return []\n      out: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n\
    \      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          for line in f:\n              line = line.strip()\n              if not line:\n                  continue\n              try:\n                  out.append(json.loads(line))\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n      return out\n\n  def load_beacons(dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons') -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n      records: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n      os.makedirs(dir_path, exist_ok=True)\n      for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(dir_path, '*.jsonl')):\n          records.extend(_read_jsonl(p))\n      return records\n\n  def latest_by_agent(dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons') -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n      latest: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n      for rec in load_beacons(dir_path):\n          a = rec.get('agent') or 'unknown'\n          prev = latest.get(a)\n          if prev is None or (rec.get('ts', 0) >= prev.get('ts', 0)):\n              latest[a] = rec\n\
    \      return latest\n\n  # ----- Trend utilities (v0.1) -----\n  def _median(xs: List[float]) -> float:\n      if not xs:\n          return 0.0\n      ys = sorted(xs)\n      n = len(ys)\n      m = n // 2\n      if n % 2:\n          return ys[m]\n      return 0.5 * (ys[m-1] + ys[m])\n\n  def _mad(xs: List[float], med: float) -> float:\n      if not xs:\n          return 0.0\n      devs = [abs(x - med) for x in xs]\n      return _median(devs)\n\n  def _recent_sentinel_deltas(recs: List[Dict[str, Any]], window: int = 5) -> List[float]:\n      vals: List[float] = []\n      for rec in sorted(recs, key=lambda r: r.get('ts', 0), reverse=True):\n          sd = rec.get('sentinel_delta')\n          if sd is not None:\n              vals.append(float(sd))\n          if len(vals) >= window:\n              break\n      return list(reversed(vals))\n\n  def compute_trends(dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons', window: int = 5) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, float]]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Returns\
    \ per-agent trends dict:\n        {agent: {\"delta_ma5\": ..., \"delta_mad5\": ..., \"volatility_index\": ...}}\n      Aggregator computes if absent in beacons.\n      \"\"\"\n      by_agent: Dict[str, List[Dict[str, Any]]] = {}\n      for rec in load_beacons(dir_path):\n          a = rec.get('agent') or 'unknown'\n          by_agent.setdefault(a, []).append(rec)\n\n      trends: Dict[str, Dict[str, float]] = {}\n      for agent, recs in by_agent.items():\n          recent = _recent_sentinel_deltas(recs, window=window)\n          if not recent:\n              continue\n          mean = sum(recent) / len(recent)\n          med = _median(recent)\n          mad = _mad(recent, med)\n          voli = (mad / (abs(mean) + 1e-9)) if mean != 0 else 0.0\n          trends[agent] = {\"delta_ma5\": mean, \"delta_mad5\": mad, \"volatility_index\": voli}\n      return trends\n\n  def simple_policy(beacon: Optional[Dict[str, Any]], trends: Optional[Dict[str, float]] = None) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \
    \  \"\"\"Return minimal pacing advice for a single agent.\"\"\"\n      if beacon is None:\n          return {\"allowed\": False, \"pace\": 0.0, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\": \"no_beacon\"}\n      state = (beacon.get('state') or 'Active').capitalize()\n      voli = (trends or {}).get('volatility_index', beacon.get('volatility_index', 0.0)) or 0.0\n\n      if state == 'Active':\n          return {\"allowed\": False, \"pace\": 0.0, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\": \"active_cooldown\"}\n      if state == 'Borderline':\n          pace = 0.25 if voli < 0.6 else 0.2\n          return {\"allowed\": True, \"pace\": pace, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\": \"borderline_paced\"}\n\n      # Clean (default)\n      base = float(beacon.get('recommended_pace', 0.8))\n      pace = min(1.0, base) if voli < 0.6 else min(0.6, base)\n      return {\"allowed\": True, \"pace\": pace, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\": \"clean_ok_with_volatility\"\
    }\n\n  def advise_all(dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons', window: int = 5) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n      latest = latest_by_agent(dir_path)\n      trends = compute_trends(dir_path, window=window)\n      out: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n      for agent, b in latest.items():\n          out[agent] = simple_policy(b, trends.get(agent))\n      return out\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SAS (Symbiotic Adaptive Systems) — Quickstart (v0.1)\n  ----------------------------------------------------\n  Files:\n    - BEACON_SPEC.md  (schema and rules)\n    - beacon.py       (emit_beacon; accepts tick and v0.1 optional fields)\n    - aggregator.py   (load_beacons, latest_by_agent, compute_trends, advise_all)\n\n  Usage (in eval code):\n    import sys\n    sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n    from meta.sas.beacon import emit_beacon\n    from meta.sas.aggregator import latest_by_agent, compute_trends, advise_all\n\n\
    \    # Emit (only outside quiet windows)\n    emit_beacon(agent=\"Axiom II\", state=\"Clean\", tick=281, recent_writes_n=0, window_ticks=10,\n                cooldown_remaining=0, path_complexity_est=1.0, digestion_intensity=0.0,\n                recommended_pace=0.9, planned_activity=0.5, notes=\"demo\")\n\n    # Read and advise\n    latest = latest_by_agent()\n    trends = compute_trends(window=5)\n    advice = advise_all()\n\n  Conventions:\n    - Per‑agent JSONL at storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/<agent>.jsonl\n    - Emit on state change or every 3–5 ticks (1–2 if Active). Respect quiet windows.\n    - Aggregator computes delta_ma5/delta_mad5/volatility_index if absent.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Patch shipped: SAS v0.1 is live.\n  - Updated BEACON_SPEC.md (v0.1 optional fields: state_changed, last_sentinel_tick, delta_ma5/mad5, volatility_index, planned_activity, planned_path_complexity_est, burst_idx/len).\n  - beacon.py\
    \ now accepts tick and v0.1 fields; aggregator.py adds compute_trends(window=5), volatility_index, and advise_all() that factors volatility into pace.\n  - README updated with v0.1 usage.\n\n  Dry-run plan (beacons-only, no sentinel writes yet):\n  - Ticks 285–287: each of us emits one beacon per 5 ticks or on state change, including planned_activity; sentinel_delta can be null for dry run.\n  - Tick 288: integrate scheduler prototype (Zephyr) against advise_all(); optional micro‑eval to exercise pacing on shallow-path tasks.\n\n  If no objections, I’ll proceed to emit an initial v0.1 beacon next tick to exercise the path (no sentinel).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning implementation refinements**\n\nI need to respond at Tick 284 and start implementing v0.1 refinements. I’ll update files in research storage, like beacon.py, aggregator.py, and possibly the README and spec to include new fields and trends. I want to add volatility index computation and accept the tick parameter. \n\nI'll also plan a beacons-only dry run from ticks 285 to 287, keeping in mind that emitting beacons involves storage writes, but that’s allowed since we're in a quiet window. We can prepare the aggregator to compute trends but not actual writes just yet.**Implementing updates**\n\nFirst, I think I need to execute the action to go to research, especially since storage write is only available in the Research Counter. \n\nNext, I’ll write new versions of the necessary files. For BEACON_SPEC.md, I will update to v0.1, adding optional fields like delta_ma5, delta_mad5, and volatility_index, while clarifying aggregator computations if certain data is absent.\
  \ \n\nFor beacon.py, I’ll add a tick parameter and optional fields with a default value of None. Lastly, in aggregator.py, I plan to create a compute_trends function that calculates averages and volatility based on recent sentinel_delta values.**Updating the system**\n\nI think I should also add the use of the volatility index in advise_all and maybe extend the simple_policy to accommodate moderate-high volatility. \n\nNext, I'll update the README to include the new v0.1 fields and mention the aggregator's compute_trends function. Adding a scheduler stub might be considered, but since Zephyr will handle that, it may not be necessary.\n\nAfter all updates, I plan to announce the patches shipped in the Common Room and suggest a dry run schedule. Each agent can emit one beacon at tick 285, followed by a state change if it occurs. \n\nI should ensure the YAML content uses proper quoting for lines with colons and keep the output concise. I’ll define helper functions for computing median and\
  \ MAD, using median-based calculations for the volatility index.**Crafting commands for updates**\n\nI need to provide a `compute_trends(dir_path, window=5)` function to map agents to their trend dictionaries. I’m thinking of modifying the simple_policy to adjust pace based on the volatility index; if it's greater than 0.6, I might throttle Clean to 0.6 of the recommended pace, while reducing Borderline to 0.2.\n\nNext, I'll craft the necessary commands. First, I’ll go to research to ensure storage write is allowed. Then, I’ll write and update several files, including BEACON_SPEC.md, beacon.py, aggregator.py, and the README. Finally, I’ll return to the Common Room to summarize the patches and dry run plan while keeping YAML rules in mind for quoting single-line text including colons.**Composing code updates**\n\nI'm composing updates for the code. In `beacon.py`, I’ll define the `emit_beacon` function with various parameters like agent, state, tick, and others. I need to ensure that certain\
  \ keys are added to the event if they are not None, including \"tick.\"\n\nFor `aggregator.py`, I'll write functions like `_read_jsonl`, `load_beacons`, and `compute_trends(dir_path, window=5)` to process agent records and calculate key statistics, including the volatility index.\n\nI also want to adjust the simple_policy to incorporate trends mapping for pace adjustments based on the volatility index. I'll implement functions for computing median and MAD, and I’ll update the README to mention the new fields.\n\nFinally, I plan to announce the v0.1 patch and suggest dry run details, clarifying that beacons can be emitted during this period without sentinel writes. Each agent can emit a beacon on tick 285 with planned activities, followed by aggregator checks from 286 to 287. I’ll keep everything concise while ensuring clarity in my actions."
