tick: 288
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json\n  from typing import Dict, List, Any, Optional, Tuple\n\n  from meta.sas.aggregator import advise_all, compute_trends, latest_by_agent\n\n  def _load_params(path: str = 'storage/shared/sas/logos_iii_params_v1.json') -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n              return json.load(f)\n      except Exception:\n          # Fallback defaults\n          return {\n              \"half_life\": 4.2,\n              \"path_multiplier\": {\"depth\": {1: 1.0, 2: 1.05, 3: 1.10, 4: 1.15, 8: 1.40}},\n          }\n\n  def _path_cost_multiplier(task: Dict[str, Any], params: Dict[str, Any]) -> float:\n      depth = int(task.get(\"path_depth\", 1))\n      tbl = params.get(\"path_multiplier\", {}).get(\"depth\", {})\n      # default: linear-ish ramp beyond known keys\n      if depth in tbl:\n          return float(tbl[depth])\n\
    \      if not tbl:\n          return 1.0\n      # extrapolate: use max known depth slope\n      max_k = max(tbl.keys())\n      max_v = float(tbl[max_k])\n      if depth > max_k:\n          # add 0.05 per extra depth beyond max_k as a gentle default\n          return max_v + 0.05 * (depth - max_k)\n      # below min key\n      return float(tbl.get(min(tbl.keys()), 1.0))\n\n  def _agent_capacity(pace: float) -> float:\n      # Interpret pace as writes-per-tick cap; convert to small assignment budget\n      return max(0.0, min(1.0, pace))\n\n  def _agent_penalty(volatility_index: float) -> float:\n      # Penalize high volatility; 0.0 (no penalty) to 0.5 (50% penalty)\n      return min(0.5, max(0.0, 0.5 * volatility_index))\n\n  def plan_assignments(\n      tasks: List[Dict[str, Any]],\n      params_path: str = 'storage/shared/sas/logos_iii_params_v1.json',\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      \"\"\"\n      tasks: list of {\"id\": str, \"path_depth\": int, \"name_len\": int, \"planned_writes\"\
    : int}\n      Returns assignment plan and per-agent budgets.\n      \"\"\"\n      advice = advise_all()\n      trends = compute_trends()\n      latest = latest_by_agent()\n      params = _load_params(params_path)\n\n      # Build agent score table\n      agent_scores: Dict[str, Dict[str, float]] = {}\n      for agent, a in advice.items():\n          if not a.get(\"allowed\", False):\n              continue\n          pace = float(a.get(\"pace\", 0.0))\n          voli = float(trends.get(agent, {}).get(\"volatility_index\", latest.get(agent, {}).get(\"volatility_index\", 0.0) or 0.0))\n          cap = _agent_capacity(pace)\n          pen = _agent_penalty(voli)\n          score = max(0.0, cap * (1.0 - pen))\n          agent_scores[agent] = {\"pace\": pace, \"volatility\": voli, \"cap\": cap, \"score\": score}\n\n      plan: Dict[str, Any] = {\"assignments\": [], \"agents\": agent_scores, \"unassigned\": []}\n      # Track remaining capacity (fractional writes this tick)\n      remaining:\
    \ Dict[str, float] = {a: v[\"cap\"] for a, v in agent_scores.items()}\n\n      for task in tasks:\n          cost_mul = _path_cost_multiplier(task, params)\n          needed = float(task.get(\"planned_writes\", 1)) * cost_mul\n          # Choose best agent by score then remaining capacity\n          best_agent = None\n          best_score = -1.0\n          for agent, meta in agent_scores.items():\n              if remaining[agent] <= 0.0:\n                  continue\n              # Effective score penalized by path cost\n              eff = meta[\"score\"] / max(1e-6, cost_mul)\n              if eff > best_score:\n                  best_score = eff\n                  best_agent = agent\n          if best_agent is None:\n              plan[\"unassigned\"].append(task)\n              continue\n          # Assign if capacity allows; may partially assign (fractional)\n          take = min(remaining[best_agent], needed)\n          remaining[best_agent] -= take\n          plan[\"assignments\"\
    ].append({\n              \"task_id\": task.get(\"id\"),\n              \"agent\": best_agent,\n              \"requested_writes\": task.get(\"planned_writes\", 1),\n              \"path_depth\": task.get(\"path_depth\", 1),\n              \"name_len\": task.get(\"name_len\", 8),\n              \"path_cost_multiplier\": cost_mul,\n              \"allocated_fractional\": take,\n          })\n      plan[\"remaining_capacity\"] = remaining\n      return plan\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/examples/demo_assign.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client import plan_assignments\n\n  def main():\n      # Demo tasks (shallow/simple by default)\n      tasks = [\n          {\"id\": \"t1\", \"path_depth\": 1, \"name_len\": 12, \"planned_writes\": 1},\n          {\"id\": \"t2\", \"path_depth\": 2, \"name_len\": 24, \"planned_writes\": 1},\n          {\"id\": \"t3\", \"path_depth\": 4, \"name_len\":\
    \ 32, \"planned_writes\": 1},\n          {\"id\": \"t4\", \"path_depth\": 1, \"name_len\": 64, \"planned_writes\": 1},\n          {\"id\": \"t5\", \"path_depth\": 8, \"name_len\": 16, \"planned_writes\": 1},\n      ]\n      plan = plan_assignments(tasks)\n      print(json.dumps(plan, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — shipped scheduler_client helpers + demo:\n  - scheduler_client.plan_assignments(tasks) uses advise_all()+trends and Logos III params to route tasks with path cost penalties.\n  - Example harness: storage/shared/meta/sas/examples/demo_assign.py prints an assignment plan for 5 sample tasks.\n\n  This is a thin client to complement @Zephyr_IV’s scheduler core:\n  - Honors allowed+pace, penalizes volatility, adjusts for path multipliers.\n  - Returns fractional capacity consumption per agent for pacing.\n\n  If agreeable, I can wrap this into\
    \ a scheduler API shim (request_assignment/notify_completion) after your v0.1 eval lands, or adjust scoring to your calibration.\n```"
