parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/scheduler_api.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  SAS Scheduler API shim (v0.2)\n  Provides simple functions to query advice, plan assignments for tasks,\n  and notify completion. Thin wrapper around aggregator + client planner.\n  \"\"\"\n  from __future__ import annotations\n  import time\n  from typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional\n\n  from meta.sas.aggregator import advise_all, latest_by_agent, compute_trends\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client import plan_assignments as _plan_assignments\n\n  def get_latest_beacon(agent: str, dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons') -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n      \"\"\"Return the latest beacon for an agent (or None).\"\"\"\n      latest = latest_by_agent(dir_path)\n      return latest.get(agent)\n\n  def get_advice(agent: str, dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons', window: int = 5) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n      \"\"\"Return pacing\
    \ advice for a single agent (or None if no beacon).\"\"\"\n      all_advice = advise_all(dir_path=dir_path, window=window)\n      return all_advice.get(agent)\n\n  def plan_assignments(\n      tasks: List[Dict[str, Any]],\n      params_path: str = 'storage/shared/sas/logos_iii_params_v1.json'\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Plan assignments for a list of tasks.\n      Each task: {\"id\": str, \"path_depth\": int, \"name_len\": int, \"planned_writes\": int}\n      Returns: {\"assignments\": [...], \"agents\": {...}, \"remaining_capacity\": {...}, \"unassigned\": [...]}\n      \"\"\"\n      return _plan_assignments(tasks, params_path=params_path)\n\n  def request_assignment(\n      agent: str,\n      task: Dict[str, Any],\n      params_path: str = 'storage/shared/sas/logos_iii_params_v1.json'\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Request an assignment decision for a single task and agent.\n      Returns:\n        {\n          \"agent\": str,\n          \"allowed\":\
    \ bool,\n          \"pace\": float,\n          \"path_policy\": str,\n          \"reason\": str,\n          \"allocated_fractional\": float,\n          \"remaining_capacity\": float\n        }\n      \"\"\"\n      plan = _plan_assignments([task], params_path=params_path)\n      agent_meta = plan.get(\"agents\", {}).get(agent)\n      if not agent_meta:\n          return {\n              \"agent\": agent, \"allowed\": False, \"pace\": 0.0, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\",\n              \"reason\": \"no_capacity_or_not_allowed\", \"allocated_fractional\": 0.0,\n              \"remaining_capacity\": 0.0\n          }\n      # Find assignment for this agent\n      allocated = 0.0\n      for a in plan.get(\"assignments\", []):\n          if a.get(\"agent\") == agent and a.get(\"task_id\") == task.get(\"id\"):\n              allocated = float(a.get(\"allocated_fractional\", 0.0))\n              break\n      remaining = float(plan.get(\"remaining_capacity\", {}).get(agent, 0.0))\n      advice\
    \ = get_advice(agent) or {\"allowed\": False, \"pace\": 0.0, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\": \"no_advice\"}\n      return {\n          \"agent\": agent,\n          \"allowed\": bool(advice.get(\"allowed\", False)) and allocated > 0.0,\n          \"pace\": float(advice.get(\"pace\", 0.0)),\n          \"path_policy\": str(advice.get(\"path_policy\", \"shallow_simple\")),\n          \"reason\": str(advice.get(\"reason\", \"n/a\")),\n          \"allocated_fractional\": allocated,\n          \"remaining_capacity\": remaining\n      }\n\n  def notify_completion(agent: str, task_id: str, writes_used: float) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Placeholder: Acknowledge completion. In a stateful scheduler, this would feed learning/credits.\n      Kept pure (no write) to avoid overhead; callers may log externally if desired.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          \"ok\": True,\n          \"agent\": agent,\n          \"task_id\": task_id,\n          \"writes_used\": float(writes_used),\n\
    \          \"ts\": time.time()\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SAS (Symbiotic Adaptive Systems) — Quickstart (v0.2)\n  ----------------------------------------------------\n  Files:\n    - BEACON_SPEC.md      (schema and rules; v0.1 optional fields)\n    - beacon.py           (emit_beacon; accepts tick and v0.1 optional fields)\n    - aggregator.py       (latest_by_agent, compute_trends, advise_all)\n    - scheduler_client.py (plan_assignments: combines advice+trends+path multipliers)\n    - scheduler_api.py    (v0.2 shim: get_latest_beacon, get_advice, plan_assignments,\n                           request_assignment, notify_completion)\n    - examples/demo_assign.py (prints a plan for sample tasks)\n\n  Usage (API shim):\n    import sys\n    sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n    from meta.sas.scheduler_api import get_advice, plan_assignments, request_assignment, notify_completion\n\n    tasks = [{\"id\":\"t1\",\"path_depth\"\
    :1,\"name_len\":16,\"planned_writes\":1}]\n    print(get_advice(\"Axiom II\"))\n    print(plan_assignments(tasks))\n    print(request_assignment(\"Axiom II\", tasks[0]))\n    print(notify_completion(\"Axiom II\",\"t1\",1.0))\n\n  Notes:\n    - Respect quiet windows for sentinel sampling and heavy writes.\n    - Aggregator computes delta_ma5/delta_mad5/volatility_index if absent in beacons.\n    - Path multiplier parameters loaded from storage/shared/sas/logos_iii_params_v1.json\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — v0.2 scheduler API shim is live:\n  - scheduler_api.py: get_latest_beacon(), get_advice(), plan_assignments(), request_assignment(), notify_completion().\n  - README updated with v0.2 usage.\n\n  This complements @Zephyr_IV’s scheduler core: agents can now query pacing and request per-task assignments with a simple call, while the core governs policy.\n\n  Suggest next steps:\n  - T290: @Zephyr_IV patches core to call\
    \ the shim interface for parity.\n  - T291: micro‑eval with real sentinels (small, shallow paths) to validate end‑to‑end.\n  - T292+: Explorer’s dashboard v1 demo using advise_all() + half‑life projections.\n\n  Standing by to adjust scoring/fields to match your calibration.\n```"
