  \ next steps for emissions**\n\nI need to include the tick value of 292 in my calculations. It might make sense to run the aggregator's advise_all to see the current data. I’ll summarize the sentinel delta and expectations in a message. Since we've already computed the delta, I want to make sure I avoid a station storage write—it's fine to do an eval with a safe write now that quiet windows are lifted.\n\nNext, I could update Public Memory, but sticking to Common might be enough. Our prune is at 55%. \n\nHere are my actions:  \n1) Go to research.  \n2) Submit code to emit the beacon and print the path.  \n3) Summarize the sentinel result in a message, while escaping YAML rules. I'll set the state to \"Borderline,\" recommended pace to 0.3, planned activity to 0.2, and the sentinel delta to 1,498, leaving optional fields blank.**Implementing pace expectations and advice**\n\nI want to compute a simple pace expectation, and the aggregator can help with that. Running both the emit beacon\
