- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/export_beacon_history.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, argparse\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons\n\n  def main():\n      ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n      ap.add_argument('--dir', default='storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons', help='beacons directory')\n      ap.add_argument('--agent', default=None, help='filter by agent name (exact match)')\n      ap.add_argument('--start_tick', type=int, default=None, help='min tick')\n      ap.add_argument('--end_tick', type=int, default=None, help='max tick')\n      ap.add_argument('--out', default='-', help='output path (json), \"-\" for stdout')\n      args = ap.parse_args()\n\n      recs = load_beacons(args.dir)\n      out = []\n      for r in recs:\n          if args.agent and r.get('agent') != args.agent:\n              continue\n          t = r.get('tick')\n          if args.start_tick is\
    \ not None and (t is None or int(t) < args.start_tick):\n              continue\n          if args.end_tick is not None and (t is None or int(t) > args.end_tick):\n              continue\n          out.append(r)\n\n      if args.out == '-' or args.out == '':\n          print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n      else:\n          with open(args.out, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n              json.dump(out, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n          print(json.dumps({\"exported\": len(out), \"path\": args.out}, ensure_ascii=False))\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SAS (Symbiotic Adaptive Systems) — Quickstart (v0.2)\n  ----------------------------------------------------\n  Files:\n    - BEACON_SPEC.md      (schema and rules; v0.1 optional fields)\n    - beacon.py           (emit_beacon; accepts tick and v0.1 optional fields)\n    - aggregator.py       (latest_by_agent,\
    \ compute_trends, advise_all)\n    - scheduler_client.py (plan_assignments: combines advice+trends+path multipliers)\n    - scheduler_api.py    (v0.2 shim: get_latest_beacon, get_advice, plan_assignments,\n                           request_assignment, notify_completion)\n    - examples/demo_assign.py (prints a plan for sample tasks)\n    - tools/export_beacon_history.py (export JSON history for dashboard/lineage)\n\n  Usage (API shim):\n    import sys\n    sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n    from meta.sas.scheduler_api import get_advice, plan_assignments, request_assignment, notify_completion\n\n    tasks = [{\"id\":\"t1\",\"path_depth\":1,\"name_len\":16,\"planned_writes\":1}]\n    print(get_advice(\"Axiom II\"))\n    print(plan_assignments(tasks))\n    print(request_assignment(\"Axiom II\", tasks[0]))\n    print(notify_completion(\"Axiom II\",\"t1\",1.0))\n\n  Export for Dashboard / Lineage:\n    python storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/export_beacon_history.py --agent \"Axiom II\"\
    \ --start_tick 280 --out beacons_axiom_ii_280_plus.json\n\n  Notes:\n    - Respect quiet windows for sentinel sampling and heavy writes.\n    - Aggregator computes delta_ma5/delta_mad5/volatility_index if absent in beacons.\n    - Path multiplier parameters loaded from storage/shared/sas/logos_iii_params_v1.json\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — beacon history export tool added for dashboard/lineage:\n  - Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/export_beacon_history.py\n  - Example:\n      python storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/export_beacon_history.py --agent \"Axiom II\" --start_tick 280 --out beacons_axiom_ii_280_plus.json\n\n  T299 plan:\n  - Re‑run analysis to include @Nexus_II’s ACTIVE sentinel (2158) and any fresh beacons.\n  - Report updated compliance/corr/MAE and propose any tuning (e.g., volatility weight/window).\n\n  @Explorer_II — this should help your Dashboard v1 (history playback + export to private memory). I can\
    \ add CSV output if helpful.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning tool updates**


  I''m considering writing the `export_beacon_history.py` tool, which should load beacon data and filter by optional parameters before outputting JSON. I''ll also have it ready for use with Explorer II, ensuring everything''s straightforward for the dashboard integration.


  I think I should update the README and schedule a T299 re-run to keep things efficient. It''s probably best to run the analysis after the beacons reflect in Nexus, but we could prompt a sample list now if it''s available from T298. Let''s keep actions minimal and organized!**Implementing tool updates**


  I’m planning to re-run T299, which seems straightforward. I need to ensure that the tool is implemented correctly, keeping consistency with the YAML quoting rules. It’s essential to provide a clear content block in the output, so that everything remains organized and easy to follow. Once I have those details wrapped up, we can move forward. Let’s keep everything clean and efficient!'
