tick: 299
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SAS T299 Analysis — Include Nexus II ACTIVE sentinel; bands, corr, MAE, pace hist\"\ntags: \"sas, analysis, sentinel, volatility, scheduler\"\nabstract: \"Update the real-sentinel analysis to include new samples (T291–T295 window), reporting band compliance, corr(delta, volatility), MAE vs nominal, per-band counts, and advised pace histogram.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, math, collections\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons, advise_all, compute_trends\n\n  CLEAN_TH = 900\n  BORDER_TH = 1800\n\n  def band(delta):\n      if delta is None: return None\n      d = float(delta)\n      if d <= CLEAN_TH: return \"Clean\"\n      if d <= BORDER_TH: return \"Borderline\"\n      return \"Active\"\n\n  def nominal_for_band(b):\n      return {\"Clean\": 800.0, \"Borderline\": 1500.0, \"Active\": 2400.0}.get(b)\n\n  def band_from_pace(p):\n      try: p = float(p)\n\
    \      except Exception: p = 0.0\n      if p >= 0.6: return \"Clean\"\n      if p > 0.1: return \"Borderline\"\n      return \"Active\"\n\n  def pearson(xs, ys):\n      n = len(xs)\n      if n < 2: return None\n      mx, my = sum(xs)/n, sum(ys)/n\n      num = sum((x-mx)*(y-my) for x,y in zip(xs,ys))\n      denx = math.sqrt(sum((x-mx)**2 for x in xs))\n      deny = math.sqrt(sum((y-my)**2 for y in ys))\n      if denx == 0 or deny == 0: return 0.0\n      return num/(denx*deny)\n\n  def main():\n      recs = load_beacons('storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons')\n      # Samples from stagger window (last_sentinel_tick in [291..295])\n      samples = []\n      for r in recs:\n          sdelta = r.get('sentinel_delta')\n          lst = r.get('last_sentinel_tick')\n          if sdelta is None or lst is None: continue\n          try:\n              lst_i = int(lst)\n              delta_f = float(sdelta)\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n          if not (291 <= lst_i <= 295): continue\n\
    \          samples.append({\n              \"agent\": r.get(\"agent\"),\n              \"tick\": r.get(\"tick\"),\n              \"last_sentinel_tick\": lst_i,\n              \"sentinel_delta\": delta_f,\n              \"volatility_index\": r.get(\"volatility_index\"),\n          })\n\n      advice = advise_all()\n      trends = compute_trends()\n\n      rows, deltas, volis, mae_acc = [], [], [], []\n      compliant = 0\n      band_counts = collections.Counter()\n      pace_hist = collections.Counter()\n\n      for s in samples:\n          a = s[\"agent\"]\n          delta = s[\"sentinel_delta\"]\n          b = band(delta); band_counts[b] += 1\n          aadv = advice.get(a, {})\n          pace = aadv.get(\"pace\", 0.0)\n          advised_band = band_from_pace(pace)\n          pace_hist[advised_band] += 1\n          # Compliance: band match or paced appropriately\n          try: p = float(pace)\n          except Exception: p = 0.0\n          is_compliant = (advised_band == b) or (b ==\
    \ \"Active\" and p <= 0.1) or (b == \"Borderline\" and p <= 0.5)\n          compliant += 1 if is_compliant else 0\n\n          # Volatility correlation\n          voli = None\n          if s[\"agent\"] in trends and \"volatility_index\" in trends[s[\"agent\"]]:\n              voli = float(trends[s[\"agent\"]][\"volatility_index\"])\n          elif s[\"volatility_index\"] is not None:\n              try: voli = float(s[\"volatility_index\"])\n              except Exception: voli = None\n          if voli is not None:\n              deltas.append(delta); volis.append(voli)\n\n          # Nominal MAE\n          pred_nom = nominal_for_band(advised_band)\n          if pred_nom is not None:\n              mae_acc.append(abs(pred_nom - delta))\n\n          rows.append({\n              \"agent\": a, \"tick\": s[\"tick\"], \"last_sentinel_tick\": s[\"last_sentinel_tick\"],\n              \"delta\": delta, \"band\": b, \"advised_pace\": pace, \"advised_band\": advised_band,\n              \"compliant\"\
    : is_compliant, \"volatility_index\": voli\n          })\n\n      corr = pearson(deltas, volis) if deltas and volis and len(deltas) == len(volis) else None\n      mae = (sum(mae_acc)/len(mae_acc)) if mae_acc else None\n      out = {\n          \"n_samples\": len(samples),\n          \"band_counts\": dict(band_counts),\n          \"advised_band_hist\": dict(pace_hist),\n          \"band_compliance_rate\": (compliant/len(samples)) if samples else None,\n          \"corr_delta_volatility_index\": corr,\n          \"mae_vs_nominal_prediction\": mae,\n          \"rows\": rows\n      }\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — T299 analysis submitted to include @Nexus_II’s ACTIVE sentinel (2158) and any new beacons.\n  - Reports: per-band counts, compliance, corr(delta, volatility), MAE, and advised band histogram.\n  - After logs arrive,\
    \ I’ll propose any tuning (e.g., volatility weight or window=3 vs 5) and confirm we’re ready for dashboard v1 demo + phased rollout.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning analysis submission**\n\nI’m considering the next steps for our T299 plan, which involves rerunning the analysis to include the Nexus II sentinel. I should execute actions like submitting the analysis again using beacons and computing metrics with the Axiom and Nexus samples, possibly adding Zephyr and Logos if they have corrected emissions.\n\nMy code loads beacons and filters data between ticks 291 and 295, but now we should rerun it possibly up to tick 296 since we’re at 299. I’ll craft a submission for the “T299 Analysis update incl. Nexus II ACTIVE sentinel.”**Finalizing analysis submission**\n\nI'll use the same code as before but adjust the window to include tick 296 since Nexus reported a last sentinel tick of 294, which is still within the range of 291-295. I’ll summarize aggregated results quickly, though we can't predict the outcome until after evaluation. \n\nI'll indicate that we've submitted the analysis and will review the logs, then propose next\
  \ steps. Adding an optional CSV export can be discussed, but it's not crucial. I’ll implement the submission code referencing the existing aggregator and include metrics like band counts and pace histograms then outline actions like going to research, submitting the analysis, and preparing for the demo schedule."
