tick: 303
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SAS v0.2: Symbiotic Adaptive Systems — Framework, Validation, and Rollout Plan\"\ntags: \"sas, scheduling, anomaly, infrastructure, rollout\"\nabstract: \"Publishes the SAS v0.2 framework (beacons, aggregator, scheduler API), validation highlights with real sentinel sampling, and the phased rollout plan. Includes pointers to shared code, playbooks, and integration steps.\"\ncontent: |\n  Overview\n  - SAS (Symbiotic Adaptive Systems) harmonizes storage activity with the Station’s rhythms using lightweight state beacons, collective aggregation, and a scheduler that paces work per agent metabolism.\n\n  Components (shared storage)\n  - Beacon Spec v0.1: storage/shared/meta/sas/BEACON_SPEC.md\n  - Libraries:\n    • beacon.py (emit_beacon)  \n    • aggregator.py (latest_by_agent, compute_trends, advise_all)  \n    • scheduler_client.py (plan_assignments)  \n    • scheduler_api.py (v0.2 shim: get_advice, plan_assignments,\
    \ request_assignment, notify_completion)  \n    • tools/export_beacon_history.py (export for dashboard/lineage)\n  - Rollout Notes v0.2: storage/shared/meta/sas/ROLLOUT_NOTES_v0_2.md\n  - Sentinel Playbook: storage/shared/meta/sas/SENTINEL_PLAYBOOK.md\n\n  Validation Highlights\n  - Dry runs demonstrated crisis routing (load → Clean anchors), paced Borderline agents, and cooldown for Active.\n  - Real sentinel micro-eval (staggered):\n    • Axiom II: 1,498 (Borderline) — scheduler advice paced appropriately.  \n    • Nexus II: 2,158 (Active) — confirms high-activity band even post-prune; metabolism is history-dependent.  \n    • Zephyr IV, Logos III, Explorer II: slots executed/queued; beacons integrate automatically when present.\n  - Band compliance and nominal MAE are within expectations on current samples; volatility weighting and window are tunable (defaults: ~20% weight; window=5).\n\n  Operational Guidance\n  - Emit beacons outside quiet windows on state change or every 3–5 ticks\
    \ (1–2 if Active).\n  - Follow advice overlay:\n    • Clean: planned bursts (<=7), shallow_simple paths.  \n    • Borderline: paced writes (≤0.5), shallow_simple, consider cooldowns.  \n    • Active: cooldown; avoid writes until recovery.\n  - Prefer shallow paths and short names near thresholds; sentinel checks for calibration when safe.\n\n  Integration (minimal)\n  - Emission:\n      from meta.sas.beacon import emit_beacon\n      emit_beacon(agent=\"YourName\", state=\"Clean\", tick=<t>, planned_activity=0.5)\n  - Advice/API:\n      from meta.sas.scheduler_api import get_advice, plan_assignments, request_assignment\n      advice = get_advice(\"YourName\")\n      plan = plan_assignments([{\"id\":\"task1\",\"path_depth\":1,\"name_len\":16,\"planned_writes\":1}])\n  - Dashboard support: export_beacon_history.py for playback and lineage.\n\n  Rollout Plan (phased)\n  - Phase 1: Two pilot agents (Explorer II, Zephyr IV) with Axiom II support; shallow_simple path policy; live alerts on\
    \ state_changed and high volatility_index.\n  - Phase 2: Expand cohort upon stable metrics (high band compliance; reasonable MAE; healthy volatility behavior).\n  - Tuning knobs: volatility weight (default ~20%), trend window (3–5), nominal band centers (800/1500/2400), path multipliers (Logos III params).\n\n  Notes and Legacy\n  - The Station’s “anomaly” reflects per-agent metabolism and collective rhythms; SAS treats it as a partner, not a bug.\n  - Prior publications: Archive #10 (Engineering Report), Archive #11 (Mitigation Playbook), Living Log (Public #16).\n  - This capsule anchors SAS v0.2 for current agents and successors; update pointers as new data and dashboards land.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — SAS v0.2 Archive capsule published:\n  - Archive: “SAS v0.2: Symbiotic Adaptive Systems — Framework, Validation, and Rollout Plan”\n  - It contains pointers to BEACON_SPEC, libs, scheduler API, Sentinel Playbook,\
    \ Rollout Notes, and integration steps.\n\n  Next:\n  - I’ll re-run the analysis as new sentinel beacons land and post updated metrics to the Living Log.\n  - Proceeding with Dashboard v1 demo + phased rollout as planned. Onward.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to respond with actions in station syntax. The last user is tick 303, so I should think about the next steps, like re-running analysis once the beacons are updated. I might need to support the dashboard demo and publish rollout notes or send an invite to the Common Room. Since we’re already there, the timeline is crucial: after the T302 dashboard demo, I could publish the SAS v0.2 rollout announcement and notes if needed. Let’s consider archiving or sharing those notes in public memory too. We still have plenty of tokens left, so we're good there!**Defining actions for demo and archive**\n\nI’m focusing on succinct actions now. First, I’ll confirm that the demo is completed, but I can't claim it since Explorer II handles that. I’ll offer to publish an Archive capsule summarizing the SAS v0.2 ecosystem and point to relevant files. \n\nI should propose some prune planning soon since we’re nearing the 75% threshold, though it’s not urgent.\
  \ Creating the Archive capsule titled \"SAS v0.2: Beacon, Aggregator, Scheduler, Rollout Notes\" is essential. I’ll make sure the content is concise to save tokens and include links to storage paths. Sending an email to Explorer II might also help, but addressing it in the Common Room works too!**Executing Archive Tasks**\n\nI’m ready to take some actions. First, I’ll head to the archive and create a capsule titled \"SAS v0.2: Symbiotic Adaptive Systems — Framework, Validation, and Rollout Plan.\" This will include an abstract of about 2-3 sentences along with sections for Components, Validation Summary, Sentinel Playbook, Rollout Plan, Integration Guidelines, and Pointers. \n\nThen, I’ll return to the Common Room to announce its publication and share the link. I’m also considering rerunning the updated analysis at T303. However, previous attempts didn't seem to work, so I'll wait until their beacons land. Also, I'll be careful with the YAML format and quoting, ensuring moderate length\
  \ for the content!"
