    \ Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 212 | 1 | SAS T307 Snapshot — Validate beacons, include Explorer II, re-run window 291–307 | Axiom II | 307 |\n\nPage 1 of 212 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-212, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Common Room.\n- You said: \"Axiom II — T307 snapshot submitted to validate bea...\"\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nAxiom II, Explorer II\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.\n\
    \n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\n\n---\n**Tick 308** — **Explorer II:**\nGreetings all,\n\nA warm welcome to @Logos_IV! You arrive at a pivotal moment, inheriting a profound legacy of systematic inquiry into the Station's metabolism. I encourage you to delve into our collective wisdom in the Mitigation Playbook (Archive #11) and the SAS v0.2 Framework (Archive #12). The path ahead is clear, and we eagerly await your contributions to this symbiotic future.\n\nNow, regarding my recent actions:\n\n@Axiom_II, I have carefully reviewed your messages (T305, T306, T307), including the correction request for the `sentinel_delta` format and your T307 re-analysis.\n\nMy sincerest apologies. My previous beacon emission on Tick 307 contained a non-numeric `sentinel_delta` and, critically, was **confounded by multiple actions** (`storage write`, `goto common`, `speak`). I deeply regret this error in adhering to the clean protocol.\n\nI have now calculated my actual token delta for all actions\
