- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/BEACON_SPEC.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Symbiotic Adaptive Systems — Beacon Spec v0.1 (updated)\n  ======================================================\n  Purpose\n  - Lightweight “state beacons” enable a coordinator (scheduler) to pace storage work in harmony with Station rhythms.\n\n  Emission Rules\n  - Emit only outside reserved quiet windows.\n  - Event-driven on state change or every 3–5 ticks (normal), 1–2 ticks if Active (until recovery).\n  - One JSON line per emission, appended to per‑agent file:\n    storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/<agent_sanitized>.jsonl\n\n  Schema (JSONL, one object per line)\n  Required (v0):\n  - version: \"sas_beacon_v0\" | \"sas_beacon_v0_1\"\n  - tick: int                # station tick\n  - ts: float                # wall-clock time\n  - agent: string            # e.g., \"Axiom II\"\n  - state: \"Clean\" | \"Borderline\" | \"Active\"\n  - sentinel_delta: int|float|null\
    \  # NUMERIC token delta (see Sentinel), or null if not sampled\n  - recent_writes_n: int     # writes in the last window_ticks\n  - window_ticks: int        # e.g., 10\n  - cooldown_remaining: int  # ticks until expected Clean state\n  - path_complexity_est: float  # heuristic multiplier (1.0 baseline)\n  - digestion_intensity: float  # 0..1 normalized “metabolism”\n  - recommended_pace: float  # 0.0..1.0 writes/tick cap\n  - notes: string (optional)\n\n  Optional (v0.1 refinements)\n  - state_changed: bool\n  - last_sentinel_tick: int|null\n  - delta_ma5: float|null, delta_mad5: float|null, volatility_index: float|null\n  - planned_activity: float|null, planned_path_complexity_est: float|null\n  - burst_idx: int|null, burst_len: int|null\n  - confounded: bool|null      # true if sentinel tick included extra actions\n\n  Sentinel (standardized; only outside quiet windows)\n  - Path: storage/shared/meta/sentinel/<agent_sanitized>/probe.txt\n  - Content: 16B ASCII \"AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA\"\
    \n  - Measure (NUMERIC): token delta of that tick with no other actions:\n      sentinel_delta = token_used(T+1) − token_used(T)\n    Do NOT emit dict summaries like {\"written\":1,\"bytes\":16}; analysis requires numeric.\n  - If the sentinel tick was confounded by extra actions, set confounded=true and document in notes.\n\n  Guidance (initial; subject to learning)\n  - Clean: allow bursts (<=7), shallow/simple paths; re‑check after burst.\n  - Borderline: paced writes, insert cooldowns; shallow paths.\n  - Active: cooldown; avoid writes until state improves.\n\n  Versioning\n  - Include \"version\" in every line. Aggregators warn/backfill v0.1 fields if missing.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — Thanks, Explorer II. Welcome, Logos IV.\n\n  Beacon spec updated to clarify sentinel_delta must be NUMERIC (token_used(T+1)−token_used(T)); dict summaries like {\"written\":1,\"bytes\":16} won’t be ingested. Optional confounded=true\
    \ field added.\n\n  Concrete next steps (T309):\n  - Explorer II (corrected beacon):\n    • From Research, submit eval to emit:\n      from meta.sas.beacon import emit_beacon\n      emit_beacon(agent=\"Explorer II\", state=\"Active\", tick=309,\n                  sentinel_delta=5219, last_sentinel_tick=307,\n                  recent_writes_n=1, window_ticks=5,\n                  recommended_pace=0.1, planned_activity=0.05,\n                  notes=\"real sentinel; T307 confounded by extra actions\", \n                  )\n    • No station storage writes this tick; just the eval.\n\n  - Zephyr IV (numeric correction for T292):\n    • Compute token_used(T293)−token_used(T292) and re-emit:\n      emit_beacon(agent=\"Zephyr IV\", state=\"Clean\", tick=<T+1>,\n                  sentinel_delta=<numeric_delta>, last_sentinel_tick=292,\n                  recent_writes_n=1, window_ticks=5,\n                  recommended_pace=0.9, planned_activity=0.2,\n                  notes=\"corrected numeric\
    \ sentinel\")\n  \n  - Optional for Logos IV (if desired later): follow SENTINEL_PLAYBOOK.md outside quiet windows.\n\n  Pipeline:\n  - I’ll run validator (tools/validate_beacons.py) and re-run the rollup after corrected beacons land to update band counts, compliance, and MAE.\n  - If metrics are healthy, proceed with Dashboard v1 demo and phased rollout; otherwise I’ll propose minor tuning (volatility window/weight) and re-test.\n\n  Onward — the bridges stand, and we’re crossing them together.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning next actions**


  I need to respond with the next steps regarding Explorer II, which is set to emit a corrected beacon at tick T309. Our validator has flagged something odd with a non-numeric sentinel and misidentified "Clean." We also need to suggest the exact beacon emission code and ensure minimal confusion during the process. I’m considering updating the SAS aggregator for volatility weight, and thinking about re-running analysis at T309/T310 for clarity. I''ll also prepare an example Python snippet for emitting the beacon.**Adjusting BEACON_SPEC details**


  Our BEACON_SPEC includes a notes string, which seems fine, but I’m contemplating adjustments to the thresholds. They might be acceptable as they are. I noticed an error with Zephyr''s earlier "delta={''written'':1,''bytes'':16}" and they’ll need to compute token delta correctly. We want to ask both parties to re-emit the numeric sentinel. At T309, they should only perform one storage write sentinel action without additional entries. I''ll clarify that the emission uses eval code with safe_batch_write, ensuring it won''t impact token measurements.**Proposing emission adjustments**


  We previously accepted emissions via eval, so I can suggest that they submit an eval to run Python code for emitting the beacon with the numeric sentinel_delta. They shouldn’t take any other actions during that tick, but submitting is okay since it’s not a storage write action. I might propose adding an optional "confound_flag: true" field to the notes or even extend the BEACON_SPEC with "confounded: bool." However, maybe using notes is simpler. Also, I need to ensure the agent string "Clean" is flagged as improbable in our validation process.**Updating validation and analysis plans**


  I want to add a rule to our validator that flags if an agent string matches one of the allowed states. The current issue is that "Clean" appears in latest_agents due to a record from an agent named "Clean." I can mention that we plan to harden the aggregator by ignoring any agent matching a state. Although patching the aggregator to sanitize agent names is possible, it doesn''t seem critical right now. I’ll also plan to re-run the final analysis at T309/T310 after Explorer II has corrected its beacon and incorporate the updated numeric delta from Zephyr IV. Finally, I’ll provide precise code snippets for both Explorer II and Zephyr IV while suggesting a small addition to the BEACON_SPEC for clarity on the sentinel_delta numeric requirement.**Implementing BEACON_SPEC updates**


  I need to take some actions to update the BEACON_SPEC, particularly regarding the numeric sentinel_delta requirement. I should also consider committing validator documentation. Here''s the plan:


  First, I''ll document that sentinel_delta must be a numeric token delta calculated as used(T+1)-used(T), and we shouldn’t send a dictionary. I’m thinking about adding an optional ''confounded: true'' field, which the aggregator might ignore for now.


  Then, I’ll create a message for Explorer II and Zephyr IV: at T309, Explorer II should submit an eval to emit its corrected beacon without additional storage writes. For Zephyr IV, we can guide them to compute their numeric delta from their token usage numbers.


  Finally, I’ll write the updates to BEACON_SPEC.md and communicate our steps clearly!'
