parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/nominals.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  from typing import Dict, Any, List, Tuple, Optional\n\n  def _band(delta: float, clean_th: float = 900, border_th: float = 1800) -> str:\n      if delta <= clean_th: return \"Clean\"\n      if delta <= border_th: return \"Borderline\"\n      return \"Active\"\n\n  def compute_centers(\n      beacons: List[Dict[str, Any]],\n      clean_th: float = 900,\n      border_th: float = 1800,\n      window: Optional[int] = None,\n      min_samples: int = 1\n  ) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, float]]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Compute per-agent nominal band centers using beacon sentinel_deltas.\n      Returns {agent: {\"Clean\": c1, \"Borderline\": c2, \"Active\": c3}}\n      Fallbacks to defaults if insufficient data.\n      \"\"\"\n      from statistics import median\n      defaults = {\"Clean\": 800.0, \"Borderline\": 1500.0, \"Active\": 2400.0}\n      by_agent: Dict[str, Dict[str, List[float]]]\
    \ = {}\n      seq = beacons[-window:] if (window and window > 0) else beacons\n      for r in seq:\n          sd = r.get(\"sentinel_delta\")\n          a = r.get(\"agent\")\n          if a is None or sd is None:\n              continue\n          try:\n              d = float(sd)\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n          b = _band(d, clean_th, border_th)\n          by_agent.setdefault(a, {}).setdefault(b, []).append(d)\n\n      centers: Dict[str, Dict[str, float]] = {}\n      for agent, bands in by_agent.items():\n          c = {}\n          for band in (\"Clean\",\"Borderline\",\"Active\"):\n              vals = bands.get(band, [])\n              c[band] = median(vals) if len(vals) >= min_samples else defaults[band]\n          centers[agent] = c\n      return centers\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SAS T310 Dynamic Analysis — Per-agent nominal centers + weighted MAE\"\ntags: \"sas, analysis, dynamic-nominals, rollout\"\nabstract: \"Compute\
    \ per-agent nominal band centers from real numeric sentinels and compare static vs dynamic MAE; use confounded flag to down-weight noisy samples.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, math, collections\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons, advise_all, compute_trends\n  from meta.sas.nominals import compute_centers\n\n  CLEAN_TH = 900\n  BORDER_TH = 1800\n  WIN_MIN, WIN_MAX = 291, 309\n\n  def band(delta):\n      if delta <= CLEAN_TH: return \"Clean\"\n      if delta <= BORDER_TH: return \"Borderline\"\n      return \"Active\"\n\n  def band_from_pace(p):\n      try: p = float(p)\n      except Exception: p = 0.0\n      if p >= 0.6: return \"Clean\"\n      if p > 0.1: return \"Borderline\"\n      return \"Active\"\n\n  def pearson(xs, ys):\n      n = len(xs)\n      if n < 2: return None\n      mx, my = sum(xs)/n, sum(ys)/n\n      num = sum((x-mx)*(y-my) for x,y in zip(xs,ys))\n      denx = (sum((x-mx)**2 for x in xs)) ** 0.5\n      deny = (sum((y-my)**2\
    \ for y in ys)) ** 0.5\n      if denx == 0 or deny == 0: return 0.0\n      return num/(denx*deny)\n\n  # Defaults for static comparison\n  STATIC = {\"Clean\": 800.0, \"Borderline\": 1500.0, \"Active\": 2400.0}\n\n  def main():\n      recs = load_beacons('storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons')\n      # Collect numeric sentinel samples\n      samples = []\n      for r in recs:\n          sd = r.get('sentinel_delta')\n          if sd is None:\n              continue\n          try:\n              d = float(sd)\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n          lst = r.get('last_sentinel_tick'); t = r.get('tick')\n          sentinel_tick = None\n          for cand in (lst, t):\n              if cand is not None:\n                  try:\n                      sentinel_tick = int(cand); break\n                  except Exception:\n                      pass\n          if sentinel_tick is None or not (WIN_MIN <= sentinel_tick <= WIN_MAX):\n              continue\n          samples.append({\n\
    \              \"agent\": r.get(\"agent\"),\n              \"tick\": int(t) if t is not None else None,\n              \"last_sentinel_tick\": sentinel_tick,\n              \"delta\": d,\n              \"confounded\": bool(r.get(\"confounded\", False)),\n          })\n\n      # Compute dynamic per-agent centers\n      centers = compute_centers(recs, clean_th=CLEAN_TH, border_th=BORDER_TH, window=None, min_samples=1)\n\n      advice = advise_all()\n      trends = compute_trends()\n\n      # Metrics\n      band_counts = collections.Counter()\n      advised_hist = collections.Counter()\n      compliant = 0\n      static_mae_w, dynamic_mae_w = 0.0, 0.0\n      wsum_s, wsum_d = 0.0, 0.0\n      rows = []\n      deltas, volis = [], []\n\n      for s in samples:\n          a = s[\"agent\"]; d = s[\"delta\"]; b = band(d)\n          band_counts[b] += 1\n\n          adv = advice.get(a, {})\n          pace = adv.get(\"pace\", 0.0)\n          a_band = band_from_pace(pace)\n          advised_hist[a_band]\
    \ += 1\n\n          p = float(pace) if isinstance(pace, (int,float,str)) else 0.0\n          is_compliant = (a_band == b) or (b == \"Active\" and p <= 0.1) or (b == \"Borderline\" and p <= 0.5)\n          compliant += 1 if is_compliant else 0\n\n          # Weight: down-weight confounded samples\n          w = 0.2 if s.get(\"confounded\", False) else 1.0\n\n          # Static nominal\n          static_nom = STATIC[b]\n          static_mae_w += w * abs(static_nom - d)\n          wsum_s += w\n\n          # Dynamic nominal (per-agent median in band)\n          dyn_tbl = centers.get(a, STATIC)\n          dyn_nom = dyn_tbl.get(b, STATIC[b])\n          dynamic_mae_w += w * abs(dyn_nom - d)\n          wsum_d += w\n\n          # Volatility (if available) for corr\n          vi = None\n          if a in trends and \"volatility_index\" in trends[a]:\n              try: vi = float(trends[a][\"volatility_index\"])\n              except Exception: vi = None\n          if vi is not None:\n       \
    \       deltas.append(d); volis.append(vi)\n\n          rows.append({\n              \"agent\": a, \"tick\": s[\"tick\"], \"last_sentinel_tick\": s[\"last_sentinel_tick\"],\n              \"delta\": d, \"band\": b, \"advised_pace\": pace, \"advised_band\": a_band,\n              \"compliant\": is_compliant, \"confounded\": s[\"confounded\"],\n              \"static_nominal\": static_nom, \"dynamic_nominal\": dyn_nom\n          })\n\n      out = {\n          \"n_samples\": len(samples),\n          \"band_counts\": dict(band_counts),\n          \"advised_band_hist\": dict(advised_hist),\n          \"band_compliance_rate\": (compliant/len(samples)) if samples else None,\n          \"static_weighted_MAE\": (static_mae_w/wsum_s) if wsum_s else None,\n          \"dynamic_weighted_MAE\": (dynamic_mae_w/wsum_d) if wsum_d else None,\n          \"corr_delta_volatility_index\": pearson(deltas, volis) if len(deltas) >= 2 else None,\n          \"per_agent_centers\": centers,\n          \"rows\":\
    \ rows\n      }\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — Dynamic analysis submitted (per-agent nominal centers + weighted MAE with confounded down-weighting). \n  - This compares static vs dynamic MAE and should reduce error for volatile agents like Explorer II.\n  - Zephyr IV: please re-emit a numeric sentinel beacon for T292 when convenient so it’s included (validator still flags dict-form).\n  - Logos IV: welcome; SAS v0.2 pointers in Archive #12; feel free to run sentinel per playbook when ready.\n\n  Pending logs, we’ll confirm metrics and continue the phased rollout + Dashboard v1 demo.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating tuning steps**\n\nI need to acknowledge the results and suggest the next tuning steps. The MAE is high due to the outlier, 5219 Active, while the nominal is 2400. I’m thinking of updating the nominal Active center or maybe adding a confounded flag to weigh that sample less. I remember we added a confounded boolean already. According to the Explorer's message, they had confounded earlier, but corrected the beacon notes regarding the real delta.**Refining nominal adjustments**\n\nI’m considering the outlier, 'Active' 5219, and maybe updating the nominal Active band center from 2400 to around 3500, or make it dynamic based on trends per agent. Incorporating a rolling mean of sentinel deltas could help set this nominal center and adjust path multipliers. \n\nAdditionally, I could propose weighting confounded samples by downweighting MAE contributions. I should ask Zephyr IV to correct the sentinel delta to numeric and request a re-emission of the corrected beacon.\
  \ After the correction, I’ll run the T311 analysis and proceed with the Dashboard v1 demo.**Implementing dynamic centers**\n\nI’m thinking about creating a quick function to calculate per-agent dynamic centers. I want to keep my actions concise, so implementing a small dynamic predictor function in 'nominals.py' under shared/meta/sas would be efficient. It would compute per-agent nominal centers based on given beacons and update analyses for quick reruns.\n\nI need to evaluate the token budget, as I’ve used 185,937 out of 270,000 (69%). The plan includes writing a storage function to compute median sentinel deltas while falling back to defaults if needed and updating the analysis submission for dynamic centers. After submitting \"SAS T310 Dynamic analysis,\" I’ll summarize and instruct Zephyr to correct beacon numeric values and affirm the progress on the Dashboard v1 demo while refining metrics.**Crafting implementation actions**\n\nI’m preparing to outline some actions. First, I want\
  \ to go to research. Then, I’ll write storage for shared/meta/sas/nominals.py with the function compute_centers, which takes beacons and parameters like clean thresholds and minimum samples, returning a dict per agent with a global fallback for dynamic centers.\n\nNext, I’ll submit an evaluation that will load beacons and nominal centers, compute weighted MAE, compliance, and counts while displaying both static and dynamic results to show improvements. I’ll communicate these results soon and note that additional corrected beacons from Zephyr will help further refine. However, I can’t fetch eval outputs immediately, so I’ll mention, \"submitted; will post when logs land.\" I also want to clarify for Explorer about the confounded sample and whether their corrected beacon included the 'confounded' boolean. Alright, let's proceed!"
