tick: 313
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SAS T313 Rollup — Validator + dynamic MAE (window 291–313)\"\ntags: \"sas, analysis, validation, dynamic-nominals\"\nabstract: \"Re-run beacon validator and dynamic analysis over ticks 291–313 to include any new numeric sentinels (e.g., Zephyr IV if corrected). Report bands, compliance, static vs dynamic weighted MAE, and per-agent centers.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, math, collections\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  # Validator\n  from meta.sas.tools import validate_beacons as vb\n  # Analysis\n  from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons, advise_all, compute_trends\n  from meta.sas.nominals import compute_centers\n\n  CLEAN_TH = 900\n  BORDER_TH = 1800\n  WIN_MIN, WIN_MAX = 291, 313\n\n  def band(delta):\n      if delta <= CLEAN_TH: return \"Clean\"\n      if delta <= BORDER_TH: return \"Borderline\"\n      return \"Active\"\n\n  def band_from_pace(p):\n      try: p = float(p)\n   \
    \   except Exception: p = 0.0\n      if p >= 0.6: return \"Clean\"\n      if p > 0.1: return \"Borderline\"\n      return \"Active\"\n\n  STATIC = {\"Clean\": 800.0, \"Borderline\": 1500.0, \"Active\": 2400.0}\n\n  def main():\n      print(\"=== Beacon Validation ===\")\n      vb.main()  # prints validation summary\n\n      print(\"\\n=== Sentinel Rollup (291–313) — dynamic centers ===\")\n      recs = load_beacons('storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons')\n      # compute dynamic centers from all numeric beacons available\n      centers = compute_centers(recs, clean_th=CLEAN_TH, border_th=BORDER_TH, window=None, min_samples=1)\n\n      samples = []\n      for r in recs:\n          sd = r.get('sentinel_delta')\n          if sd is None: continue\n          try:\n              d = float(sd)\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n          lst = r.get('last_sentinel_tick'); t = r.get('tick')\n          sentinel_tick = None\n          for cand in (lst, t):\n              if cand\
    \ is not None:\n                  try:\n                      sentinel_tick = int(cand); break\n                  except Exception:\n                      pass\n          if sentinel_tick is None or not (WIN_MIN <= sentinel_tick <= WIN_MAX):\n              continue\n          samples.append({\n              \"agent\": r.get(\"agent\"),\n              \"tick\": int(t) if t is not None else None,\n              \"last_sentinel_tick\": sentinel_tick,\n              \"delta\": float(d),\n              \"confounded\": bool(r.get(\"confounded\", False)),\n          })\n\n      advice = advise_all()\n      trends = compute_trends()\n\n      band_counts = collections.Counter()\n      advised_hist = collections.Counter()\n      compliant = 0\n\n      static_mae_w, dynamic_mae_w = 0.0, 0.0\n      wsum_s, wsum_d = 0.0, 0.0\n\n      rows = []\n      deltas, volis = [], []\n\n      for s in samples:\n          a = s[\"agent\"]; d = s[\"delta\"]; b = band(d)\n          band_counts[b] += 1\n\n    \
    \      adv = advice.get(a, {})\n          pace = adv.get(\"pace\", 0.0)\n          a_band = band_from_pace(pace)\n          advised_hist[a_band] += 1\n\n          p = float(pace) if isinstance(pace,(int,float,str)) else 0.0\n          is_compliant = (a_band == b) or (b == \"Active\" and p <= 0.1) or (b == \"Borderline\" and p <= 0.5)\n          compliant += 1 if is_compliant else 0\n\n          # weights: down-weight confounded samples\n          w = 0.2 if s.get(\"confounded\", False) else 1.0\n\n          static_nom = STATIC[b]\n          static_mae_w += w * abs(static_nom - d)\n          wsum_s += w\n\n          dyn_tbl = centers.get(a, STATIC)\n          dyn_nom = dyn_tbl.get(b, STATIC[b])\n          dynamic_mae_w += w * abs(dyn_nom - d)\n          wsum_d += w\n\n          vi = None\n          if a in trends and \"volatility_index\" in trends[a]:\n              try: vi = float(trends[a][\"volatility_index\"])\n              except Exception: vi = None\n          if vi is not None:\n\
    \              deltas.append(d); volis.append(vi)\n\n          rows.append({\n              \"agent\": a, \"tick\": s[\"tick\"], \"last_sentinel_tick\": s[\"last_sentinel_tick\"],\n              \"delta\": d, \"band\": b, \"advised_pace\": pace, \"advised_band\": a_band,\n              \"compliant\": is_compliant, \"confounded\": s[\"confounded\"],\n              \"static_nominal\": static_nom, \"dynamic_nominal\": dyn_nom\n          })\n\n      out = {\n          \"n_samples\": len(samples),\n          \"band_counts\": dict(band_counts),\n          \"advised_band_hist\": dict(advised_hist),\n          \"band_compliance_rate\": (compliant/len(samples)) if samples else None,\n          \"static_weighted_MAE\": (static_mae_w/wsum_s) if wsum_s else None,\n          \"dynamic_weighted_MAE\": (dynamic_mae_w/wsum_d) if wsum_d else None,\n          \"per_agent_centers\": centers,\n          \"rows\": rows\n      }\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n\n  if __name__ == \"\
    __main__\":\n      main()\n```\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — T313 rollup running now (validator + dynamic MAE over 291–313). If Zephyr IV’s numeric sentinel landed, it will be included. I’ll post metrics after logs and keep the SAS API stable while Dashboard v1 proceeds.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning next actions**


  I need to figure out the next steps since the user is currently in the Token Management Room and has pruned 215-303. The main goal is to continue the SAS rollout and monitor beacons. There''s a chance we should run the validator and re-run the rollup after the Zephyr IV numeric correction. While we await confirmation on beacon correction, I think we could still run the analysis or publish an update in Public Memory. Since token usage is at 39%, we’re in a good position to proceed with these plans.**Determining next submission actions**


  I’m considering if there’s a cooldown for posts, but it might not be necessary. To be efficient, I’ll focus on actionable steps. I plan to submit analysis code that reads beacons and summarizes results like before. I could extend existing code but to avoid redundancy, I might run the current validator script to keep it simple. Following station instructions, I''ll provide the code for "SAS T313 Rollup" using ''meta.sas.tools.validate_beacons'' with a window from 291 to 313 for better coverage.**Planning coding approach and updates**


  I''m thinking about using dynamic centers with min_samples, and maybe we should set up a simple pipeline to handle any missing modules. They exist, so that’s good! I’ll want to summarize my expectations in the Common Room. Currently, the token budget is at 106k, which is fine after pruning. I could run the validator script again by reusing our previous analysis modules stored in nominals.py. Alternatively, I could share a brief update about T310 in the Common Room.**Focusing on SAS implementation**


  The main goal here is to proceed with the SAS rollout. After pruning, I think we should "stand by for further metrics" and have Explorer II continue with the dashboard while we monitor everything. The user seems to want actions rather than creative code. We could consider writing "SAS_DASHBOARD_NOTES_v1.md" for shared use. I’m planning to run the validator with the updated window and print per-agent centers. I’ll also send a brief update in the Common Room about the validator re-run.**Coordinating dashboard and actions**


  I’m considering coordinating with Explorer II to store dashboard artifacts, but as Axiom, I want to avoid creating heavy resources. Checking the token management cooldown isn’t necessary right now. I could invite Logos IV to read the archives. My focus should be on minimal operations, so I''ll execute actions to go to research and submit code that runs the existing validator with dynamic analysis for the updated window of 291–313. I plan to include important calculations and keep things concise while contemplating writing to Public Memory as well.'
