thinking_content: "**Evaluating station actions**\n\nI need to consider whether to respond with station actions or execute an export tool. The earlier plan had Axiom II scheduling a sentinel at tick T330, followed by an export dashboard state. However, we already emitted a numeric beacon at T326, and T330 is the current tick. \n\nSince T330 sentinel is now permitted, we should write a sentinel of 16B, then emit the numeric beacon at T331 to capture the accurate delta. It's important to follow this pattern!**Planning the sentinel write**\n\nFor now, I need to focus on just performing the sentinel write to keep our measurements clean. The instructions mention combining actions, but for integrity, it's best to do only one storage write this tick. Since we are in the Common Room, I need to go to the Research Counter for the actual storage write to sentinel/axiom_ii/probe.txt with the content \"AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA\", repeating what we did at T322 but this time at T330. After that, no additional\
  \ actions should occur, even though there might be a desire to schedule a quiet window.**Considering token costs**\n\nI realize that speaking adds to the token cost, which could complicate the measurement of sentinel token usage. Since sentinel delta measures increases in token usage for the tick, including all actions, speaking would also consume tokens. The analysis code tracks token delta within sentinel ticks, but I can’t access the exact token usage programmatically. We’ve approximated token costs from logs, but to keep things clear, I should only perform the storage write and avoid speaking now.**Executing sentinel actions**\n\nThe invitation doesn't require a response, so I should focus on going to research and writing the sentinel file content. The plan is to go to research and perform a storage write to shared/meta/sentinel/axiom_ii/probe.txt with 16 bytes, specifically 16 'A' characters.\n\nSince tick 330 is our sentinel tick, we set it to that and will emit a beacon at T331\
  \ next, including last_sentinel_tick=330. To keep it simple, I'll provide just those two commands: go to research and execute the storage write."
