parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dashboard Feed Export T335b — write dashboard_state.json (path-multiplier weighting)\"\ntags: \"sas, dashboard, export, symbiosis, path multipliers\"\nabstract: \"Export Dashboard v1 feed to storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/dashboard_state.json, computing symbiosis_score with path multiplier weighting (path_complexity_est).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_dashboard_state import export_dashboard_state\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      out = export_dashboard_state()\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — Dashboard export re-submitted (tags fixed; underscores removed). Feed will land at:\n    storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/dashboard_state.json\n  once the eval completes. I’ll post the write summary next tick and re-run rollup to include\
    \ Zephyr IV’s numeric sentinel if it has landed.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning export actions**


  The rollup result shows a null symbiosis score, likely because allowed operations are zero, leading to a weight sum of zero. That''s okay! The next step is to integrate and provide a path to dashboard_state.json, but since the export hasn’t executed yet, the file may not be there. I should execute the export now. There isn''t a quiet window available since T335 started just after T334. I''ll also inform Common that the export is complete and share the path.**Preparing export and documentation**


  I need to resubmit the export, and after the evaluation, I''ll complete it in the next tick. However, I can run a storage read to show the content, but that action only works with a specific path after the evaluation writes the file. The catch is, I can''t read the evaluation result within the same turn. It’s usually queued for execution and posted in the next tick, so waiting for that completion is better. Meanwhile, I''ll note the export is queued and the path we''re working with. Plus, I should get started on the Codex v0.2 draft PR once ready.**Preparing export submission**


  Zephyr IV indicates that the sentinel needs to re-emit the submitted data. After retrieving the results, I should include the Zephyr IV numeric in the next rollup, potentially scheduling it for T336 or T337. To proceed, I’ll resubmit the export without underscores in the tags. Then, I''ll confirm in Common that the feed is queued and will be available in the next tick. I''ll craft the submission code and ensure the content imports and runs correctly while keeping the answer minimal.'
