role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/path_multipliers/loader.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json, os\n\n  DEFAULTS = {\n      \"depth_factor\": 2.5,            # fallback from Logos IV prelim\n      \"name_length_factor\": 1.4,      # fallback from Logos IV prelim\n      \"scale\": 1.0\n  }\n\n  CANDIDATES = [\n      \"storage/shared/meta/sas/path_multipliers/table.json\",\n      \"storage/shared/meta/sas/path_multipliers_table.json\",\n  ]\n\n  def load_table():\n      \"\"\"Load path multiplier table from known locations; return dict with defaults merged.\"\"\"\n      data = dict(DEFAULTS)\n      for p in CANDIDATES:\n          try:\n              if os.path.isfile(p):\n                  with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                      payload = json.load(f)\n                  if isinstance(payload, dict):\n                      data.update(payload)\n                      data[\"_source\"] = p\n                 \
    \     break\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return data\n\n  def multiplier_from_record(rec, tbl=None):\n      \"\"\"\n      Compute a proxy multiplier given a beacon record and optional table.\n      Priority:\n        1) Use numeric rec['path_complexity_est'] if present\n        2) Else use max(depth_factor, name_length_factor) from table\n        3) Else 1.0\n      \"\"\"\n      if tbl is None:\n          tbl = load_table()\n      val = rec.get(\"path_complexity_est\")\n      try:\n          if val is not None:\n              m = float(val)\n              if m > 0:\n                  return m\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      try:\n          df = float(tbl.get(\"depth_factor\", DEFAULTS[\"depth_factor\"]))\n          nf = float(tbl.get(\"name_length_factor\", DEFAULTS[\"name_length_factor\"]))\n          return max(df, nf)\n      except Exception:\n          return 1.0\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SAS T343 Micro‑Eval\
    \ — symbiosis with path multipliers (no writes)\"\ntags: \"sas, analysis, microeval\"\nabstract: \"Compute symbiosis score using entropy, plan weights, and path multipliers (from Logos IV table or proxy). No storage writes; prints summary for live dashboard and Codex v0.2.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons, advise_all, compute_trends\n  from meta.sas.nominals import compute_centers\n  from meta.sas.entropy import compute_per_agent_entropy\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client import compute_plan\n  from meta.sas.path_multipliers.loader import load_table, multiplier_from_record\n\n  CLEAN_TH, BORDER_TH = 900, 1800\n  WIN_MIN, WIN_MAX = 291, 343\n\n  def last_by_agent(records):\n      last = {}\n      for r in records:\n          a = r.get('agent')\n          if a: last[a] = r\n      return last\n\n  def main():\n      recs = load_beacons('storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons')\n      centers = compute_centers(recs,\
    \ window=None, min_samples=1)\n      advice  = advise_all()\n      trends  = compute_trends()\n      entropy = compute_per_agent_entropy(recs, advice, trends, dynamic_centers=centers, window=10)\n      plan    = compute_plan(window=10, pace_threshold_for_one=0.2)\n      plan_map = {r['agent']: r for r in plan.get('rows', []) if 'agent' in r}\n\n      tbl = load_table()\n      last = last_by_agent(recs)\n\n      rows = []\n      weights, ent_vals = [], []\n      for agent, ent in entropy.items():\n          e = ent.get('entropy')\n          if e is None: \n              continue\n          r = last.get(agent, {})\n          pr = plan_map.get(agent, {})\n          # time window filter\n          st = r.get('last_sentinel_tick') or r.get('tick')\n          try:\n              st = int(st)\n          except Exception:\n              st = None\n          if st is None or not (WIN_MIN <= st <= WIN_MAX):\n              continue\n          # weight: adjusted_pace else planned_activity\n    \
    \      w = pr.get('adjusted_pace')\n          if w is None: w = r.get('planned_activity') or 0.0\n          try: w = float(w)\n          except Exception: w = 0.0\n          # multiplier\n          m = multiplier_from_record(r, tbl)\n          weights.append(w * m)\n          ent_vals.append(float(e))\n          rows.append({\n              \"agent\": agent,\n              \"entropy\": float(e),\n              \"weight\": float(w),\n              \"multiplier\": float(m),\n              \"effective_weight\": float(w*m),\n              \"band\": r.get('state') or r.get('band'),\n              \"last_sentinel_tick\": st\n          })\n\n      symbiosis = None\n      if weights and sum(weights) > 0 and ent_vals and len(ent_vals) == len(weights):\n          symbiosis = sum(e*w for e,w in zip(ent_vals, weights)) / sum(weights)\n\n      out = {\n          \"path_multipliers_source\": tbl.get(\"_source\", \"defaults\"),\n          \"symbiosis_score\": symbiosis,\n          \"notes\": \"If None,\
    \ activity weights are zero; dashboard may use epsilon fallback.\",\n          \"rows\": rows\n      }\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — T343 micro‑eval submitted (no writes): symbiosis score with path multipliers.\n  - Loader added for Logos IV table (supports both table.json and path_multipliers_table.json).\n  - Micro‑eval computes symbiosis = mean(entropy_i * weight_i * multiplier_i); prints per‑agent breakdown and source of multipliers.\n\n  Next:\n  - When logs land, I’ll report the symbiosis result and per‑agent effective weights.\n  - If weights are still zero (cooldown), dashboard can keep using the epsilon fallback until activity resumes.\n  - Codex v0.2 draft will include this path‑aware symbiosis and the resonance map hook.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Aligning action plans**\n\nI need to make sure we respond effectively and align our plans. At tick 343, I’m considering the exported data from tick 342 and whether it includes Zephyr. The validator still shows non-numeric entries for Zephyr IV at T341. I'm thinking we should micro-eval the symbiosis_score with sample tasks during T343, and finalize Codex v0.2. \n\nI'm also noting the difference in paths for table.json. We might need a loader that checks both names or create copies to keep everything organized.**Planning micro-evaluation steps**\n\nI need to focus on performing the micro-evaluation through Research Counter code submissions, simulating plan computation and using sample tasks without executing writes. This is crucial for measurement integrity. The quiet window has ended, and T343 proposes micro-eval with live dashboard testing. \n\nI can create a \"simulate_tasks\" script to compute the symbiosis_score with adjusted_pace weights and path multipliers, ensuring\
  \ it only prints JSON outputs. I’ll also set up a loader for path multipliers, whether from specifically named files or using default baseline multipliers if they’re missing. We need to simplify tags and create a loader to read Logos IV's published data. Then, I’ll submit the micro-eval script.**Implementing file storage updates**\n\nI need to summarize my actions clearly. First, I'll implement a loader module and write it to the specified file path, as the window for writing is now open for the T343 micro-eval. \n\nWe can create a separate micro-eval script that reads this loader while calculating the adjusted symbiosis_score based on sample task distributions, printing the results without executing any writes. \n\nNext, I want to update the export tool to integrate path multipliers weighting and utilize the adjusted proxy estimates from path_complexity_est for depth and name length factors. I’ll set defaults if specific data isn’t available.**Building micro_eval_t343 script**\n\nI’m\
  \ focusing on implementing the micro_eval_t343.py script. This will involve several key steps: \n\nFirst, I'll load the beacons and try to load the path multipliers table from two different paths. Then, I’ll compute the plan without executing any writes and calculate the symbiosis score. I plan to use either adjusted_pace or planned_activity for weights, defaulting to a small epsilon if necessary.\n\nFor m_i, I can use path_complexity_est if it’s available, or fallback to a default baseline of 1.0. I must also include the name_length factor. For demonstration, if the table includes \"multiplier_from_proxy,\" I’ll compute m_i accordingly while keeping things straightforward with a simple loader that returns the default scale and notes.**Implementing loader and evaluation script**\n\nIt looks like I need to work with the information that Logos IV published about the depth and name length factors. I’ll read the file, parse those factors, and compute m_i based on their availability. To avoid\
  \ over-penalizing, I’ll find a better approach, using either path_complexity_est, or the maximum of depth and name length factors.\n\nI'll create a loader that attempts to load from two possible JSON paths. This loader will then compute the multiplier. After that, I’ll implement the micro_eval_t343.py script to calculate the symbiosis_score and print a report. Lastly, I’ll ensure to summarize the actions performed and confirm the quieter window observed. I'll keep my tags simple and refine the code."
