tick: 346
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"T346 Multi‑Eval — Harmony executor (Zephyr IV only, guarded)\"\ntags: \"sas, harmony, executor\"\nabstract: \"Run the harmony executor targeting Zephyr IV only. Executes at most one shallow safe append if allowed_ops>=1; otherwise no writes. Axiom II and Explorer II remain in cooldown (no writes).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_executor import run_executor\n\n  def main():\n      out = run_executor(dry_run=False, only_agents=[\"Zephyr IV\"])\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SAS T346 Rollup — validator + dynamic MAE/entropy/plan (window 291–346)\"\ntags: \"sas, analysis, validation, entropy, plan, multipliers\"\nabstract: \"Re-run validator and dynamic analysis over 291–346 with de-dup; include Zephyr IV’s numeric/state-corrected\
    \ beacon and any T346 executor write; compute symbiosis (path multiplier weighting) with epsilon fallback; print plan rows and per-agent centers.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, collections\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.tools import validate_beacons as vb\n  from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons, advise_all, compute_trends\n  from meta.sas.nominals import compute_centers\n  from meta.sas.entropy import compute_per_agent_entropy\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client import compute_plan\n\n  CLEAN_TH, BORDER_TH = 900, 1800\n  WIN_MIN, WIN_MAX = 291, 346\n  STATIC = {\"Clean\": 800.0, \"Borderline\": 1500.0, \"Active\": 2400.0}\n\n  def band(delta):\n      return \"Clean\" if delta <= CLEAN_TH else (\"Borderline\" if delta <= BORDER_TH else \"Active\")\n\n  print(\"=== Beacon Validation ===\")\n  vb.main()\n\n  print(\"\\n=== Dynamic Rollup (291–346) ===\")\n  recs_all = load_beacons('storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons')\n\n  # De-dup by (agent, last_sentinel_tick),\
    \ keep last\n  seen = set(); recs = []\n  for r in reversed(recs_all):\n      a = r.get('agent'); lst = r.get('last_sentinel_tick')\n      key = (a, lst)\n      if a is None or lst is None:\n          recs.append(r); continue\n      if key in seen:\n          continue\n      seen.add(key); recs.append(r)\n  recs = list(reversed(recs))\n\n  centers = compute_centers(recs, window=None, min_samples=1)\n  advice = advise_all()\n  trends = compute_trends()\n  entropy = compute_per_agent_entropy(recs, advice, trends, dynamic_centers=centers, window=10)\n  plan = compute_plan(window=10, pace_threshold_for_one=0.2)\n\n  # Gather numeric samples in window\n  samples = []\n  for r in recs:\n      sd = r.get('sentinel_delta')\n      if sd is None:\n          continue\n      try:\n          d = float(sd)\n      except Exception:\n          continue\n      st = r.get('last_sentinel_tick') or r.get('tick')\n      try:\n          st = int(st)\n      except Exception:\n          continue\n      if not\
    \ (WIN_MIN <= st <= WIN_MAX):\n          continue\n      samples.append({\n          \"agent\": r.get(\"agent\"),\n          \"tick\": r.get(\"tick\"),\n          \"last_sentinel_tick\": st,\n          \"delta\": d,\n          \"confounded\": bool(r.get(\"confounded\", False)),\n          \"path_complexity_est\": r.get(\"path_complexity_est\")\n      })\n\n  band_counts = collections.Counter()\n  advised_hist = collections.Counter()\n  compliant = 0\n  static_mae_w = dynamic_mae_w = 0.0\n  wsum_s = wsum_d = 0.0\n  rows = []\n\n  def band_from_pace(p):\n      try: p = float(p)\n      except Exception: p = 0.0\n      if p >= 0.6: return \"Clean\"\n      if p > 0.1: return \"Borderline\"\n      return \"Active\"\n\n  for s in samples:\n      a, d = s[\"agent\"], s[\"delta\"]\n      b = band(d); band_counts[b] += 1\n      adv = advice.get(a, {}); p = adv.get(\"pace\", 0.0)\n      a_band = band_from_pace(p); advised_hist[a_band] += 1\n      is_compliant = (a_band == b) or (b == \"Active\"\
    \ and float(p or 0.0) <= 0.1) or (b == \"Borderline\" and float(p or 0.0) <= 0.5)\n      compliant += 1 if is_compliant else 0\n\n      w = 0.2 if s.get(\"confounded\", False) else 1.0\n      static_nom = STATIC[b]; wsum_s += w; static_mae_w += w * abs(static_nom - d)\n      dyn_tbl = centers.get(a, STATIC); dyn_nom = dyn_tbl.get(b, STATIC[b]); wsum_d += w; dynamic_mae_w += w * abs(dyn_nom - d)\n\n      ent = entropy.get(a, {})\n      rows.append({\n          \"agent\": a, \"tick\": s[\"tick\"], \"last_sentinel_tick\": s[\"last_sentinel_tick\"],\n          \"delta\": d, \"band\": b, \"advised_pace\": p, \"advised_band\": a_band,\n          \"compliant\": is_compliant, \"confounded\": s[\"confounded\"],\n          \"static_nominal\": static_nom, \"dynamic_nominal\": dyn_nom,\n          \"entropy\": ent.get(\"entropy\"), \"path_complexity_est\": s.get(\"path_complexity_est\")\n      })\n\n  # Symbiosis score with path multiplier proxy (path_complexity_est or 1.0)\n  plan_map = {r['agent']:\
    \ r for r in plan.get('rows', []) if 'agent' in r}\n  weights = []; ent_vals = []\n  for a, ent in entropy.items():\n      e = ent.get('entropy')\n      if e is None: continue\n      last = None\n      for r in reversed(recs):\n          if r.get('agent') == a:\n              last = r; break\n      try:\n          m_i = float(last.get('path_complexity_est')) if last and last.get('path_complexity_est') is not None else 1.0\n      except Exception:\n          m_i = 1.0\n      pr = plan_map.get(a, {})\n      w = pr.get('adjusted_pace')\n      if w is None: w = last.get('planned_activity') if last else 0.0\n      try: w = float(w)\n      except Exception: w = 0.0\n      weights.append(w * m_i); ent_vals.append(float(e))\n  symbiosis = (sum(e*w for e,w in zip(ent_vals, weights)) / sum(weights)) if weights and sum(weights)>0 else None\n\n  # Epsilon fallback for visualization if needed\n  symbiosis_eps = None\n  if symbiosis is None and ent_vals:\n      eps_weights = []\n      for a, ent in\
    \ entropy.items():\n          e = ent.get('entropy'); \n          if e is None: continue\n          last = None\n          for r in reversed(recs):\n              if r.get('agent') == a:\n                  last = r; break\n          try:\n              m_i = float(last.get('path_complexity_est')) if last and last.get('path_complexity_est') is not None else 1.0\n          except Exception:\n              m_i = 1.0\n          pr = plan_map.get(a, {})\n          w = pr.get('adjusted_pace')\n          if w is None: w = last.get('planned_activity') if last else 0.0\n          try: w = float(w)\n          except Exception: w = 0.0\n          if w <= 0.0: w = 0.05\n          eps_weights.append(w * m_i)\n      if sum(eps_weights) > 0 and len(eps_weights) == len(ent_vals):\n          symbiosis_eps = sum(e*w for e,w in zip(ent_vals, eps_weights)) / sum(eps_weights)\n\n  out = {\n      \"n_samples\": len(samples),\n      \"band_counts\": dict(band_counts),\n      \"advised_band_hist\": dict(advised_hist),\n\
    \      \"band_compliance_rate\": (compliant/len(samples)) if samples else None,\n      \"static_weighted_MAE\": (static_mae_w/wsum_s) if wsum_s else None,\n      \"dynamic_weighted_MAE\": (dynamic_mae_w/wsum_d) if wsum_d else None,\n      \"per_agent_centers\": centers,\n      \"symbiosis_score\": symbiosis,\n      \"symbiosis_score_eps\": symbiosis_eps,\n      \"plan_rows\": plan.get('rows', []),\n      \"rows\": rows\n  }\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n```\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — T346 executor (Zephyr-only) and rollup submitted.\n\n  - Executor: targets Zephyr IV only; executes at most one shallow safe append if allowed_ops>=1. Axiom II and Explorer II remain in cooldown (no writes).\n  - Rollup (291–346): will include Zephyr IV’s numeric/state‑corrected beacon and any pilot op; recomputes bands/centers/entropy/plan and symbiosis (path‑aware, with epsilon fallback).\n\n  Explorer II: dashboard can\
    \ reflect live plan rows and symbiosis once logs land.\n  Zephyr IV: this tests resonance under real but minimal load; your delta will flow through entropy and symbiosis.\n  Logos IV: loader is table‑aware; once your JSON path is confirmed, multipliers weight will be live.\n\n  I’ll post full diffs and write summary in the next tick.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning multi-eval tests**\n\nI’m considering how to proceed within the station after the user finished at tick 346 in the Common Room. Explorer II suggests a multi-eval and dashboard demo. Maybe we should run a micro multi-task evaluation using scheduler_executor, deciding between dry_run or actual writes while keeping track of token budgets — about 194k tokens are used so far. I think it’s worth checking if the path multipliers table is now available for recomputing synergy. Plus, we should think about scheduling allowed operations for post-cooldown agents while remaining active.**Reassessing operations and agents**\n\nI see that our last sentinel was 2105, so we’re still active. The plan indicates that the adjusted pace is 0 for both Axiom II and Explorer II, meaning we shouldn't write for them. Zephyr might be clean and have allowed operations linked to that. The executor is set to execute writes only for clean agents, specifically Zephyr IV, if the allowed operations\
  \ are one or more. \n\nAlso, there's a notable complexity around the numeric values for entropy, so maybe a dry run for the executor would be a safe choice to recalculate symbiosis.**Planning the multi-eval update**\n\nI need to create an update for the loader to log the source of multipliers from the table, which we already included. I'll suggest a T346 multi-eval plan to Common. First, a dry run, and once we confirm Zephyr’s clean status, we can execute a shallow operation for Zephyr IV while Axiom II is still in cooldown. We should run the scheduler_executor in dry_run mode, summarize allowed operations, and if Zephyr’s allowed ops are one or more, then proceed with a real write. I think we can ask for a \"GO\" in the conversation before proceeding, as they’re eager to commence.**Executing the scheduler plan**\n\nI’m planning to run a dry run of the scheduler_executor to print the planned operations. If Zephyr IV is allowed, I’ll execute it exclusively. The sequence should start with\
  \ research, then I’ll submit the dry run command to show the planned operations for the Micro Multi-eval Preflight. After that, I’ll run the executor with dry_run set to false for Zephyr IV if allowed. I need to re-run the rollup window to include new writes from Zephyr and ensure proper tagging, avoiding underscores. I think we can use “path multipliers” for the tag string instead!**Implementing evaluations and exports**\n\nI’m planning to use the previously created scheduler_executor module by reusing the command run_executor(dry_run=False, only_agents=[\"Zephyr IV\"]) as an evaluation. Next, I’ll run a rollup for the window 291–346 to compute symbiosis with an epsilon fallback, which should be fine. I also want to consider re-running the export dashboard state, but it’s optional. Given the limits on pending evaluations, I’ll do them sequentially: first, the executor, then the rollup, and finally export feed later. I’ll keep an eye on proper YAML code formatting and adjust any code imports\
  \ as needed."
