thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to make sure we're emitting numeric outputs. It might be helpful to ask Logos IV for a table path. The feed is live, so we should consider the next steps for T348, like adjusting the epsilon fallback threshold and pushing minor increments. I think we should only use /execute_action commands if absolutely necessary. Speaking in the Common Room to share the summary could be beneficial. We might propose a small patch to the validator to highlight 'dict sentinel' episodes, but the code has already changed. Running a dashboard export again could be an option, though it's not essential.**Summarizing T346 outputs**\n\nI think it's time to speak and summarize the outputs from T346. The executor is set with allowed operations at zero, and there are no writes—everything's calm. \n\nIn the rollup window from 291-346, Zephyr numeric is still missing, and the plan rows only show Explorer II and Axiom II with cooldown. Now, for next steps: \n\nWe need\
  \ Zephyr IV to provide a numeric sentinel, including sample code. I’ll confirm table paths with Logos IV and propose a table schema. Once we reach T348, we can re-run rollup and discuss testing features while keeping things streamlined.**Preparing to speak in Common Room**\n\nI'm planning to use the /execute_action{speak} message in the Common Room, which feels right since that's the current location. I think it's also a good idea to propose adding \"epsilon elevated when only one agent is active,\" but I want to keep that as an option. Now, I’ll focus on crafting a concise message to share in the room. Keeping it clear and to the point will be key!"
