role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Harmony executor — Zephyr IV pilot op (guarded, T351)\"\ntags: \"sas, executor, harmony, guarded\"\nabstract: \"Re-run the harmony executor targeting Zephyr IV only. If plan grants allowed_ops>=1, perform at most one shallow safe operation; otherwise no writes. Axiom II and Explorer II remain in cooldown (no writes).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_executor import run_executor\n\n  def main():\n      out = run_executor(dry_run=False, only_agents=[\"Zephyr IV\"])\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dashboard Feed Refresh v0.1 — window 291–351 (centers/plan/symbiosis)\"\ntags: \"sas, dashboard, symbiosis, entropy, multipliers\"\nabstract: \"Refresh the dashboard feed with latest bands, centers, entropy, plan rows, and symbiosis\
    \ (path-aware with epsilon fallback) for window 291–351. Writes a single JSON file to dashboard_state.json.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json, collections, time\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons, advise_all, compute_trends\n  from meta.sas.nominals import compute_centers\n  from meta.sas.entropy import compute_per_agent_entropy\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client import compute_plan\n\n  WIN_MIN, WIN_MAX = 291, 351\n  CLEAN_TH, BORDER_TH = 900, 1800\n\n  def band(delta):\n      return \"Clean\" if delta is not None and delta <= CLEAN_TH else (\"Borderline\" if delta is not None and delta <= BORDER_TH else \"Active\")\n\n  def as_float(x):\n      try: return float(x)\n      except Exception: return None\n\n  recs_all = load_beacons('storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons')\n  recs_num = []\n  for r in recs_all:\n      sd = as_float(r.get('sentinel_delta'))\n      if sd is None: \n          continue\n      r = dict(r); r['sentinel_delta']\
    \ = sd\n      recs_num.append(r)\n\n  seen = set(); recs = []\n  for r in reversed(recs_num):\n      a = r.get('agent'); lst = r.get('last_sentinel_tick') or r.get('tick')\n      if a is None or lst is None:\n          continue\n      key = (a, int(lst))\n      if key in seen: \n          continue\n      seen.add(key); recs.append(r)\n  recs = list(reversed(recs))\n\n  samples = []\n  latest_by_agent = {}\n  for r in recs:\n      lst = r.get('last_sentinel_tick') or r.get('tick')\n      try: lst = int(lst)\n      except Exception: continue\n      if 291 <= lst <= 351:\n          samples.append(r)\n          latest_by_agent[r.get('agent')] = r\n\n  centers = compute_centers(recs, window=None, min_samples=1)\n  advice = advise_all()\n  trends = compute_trends()\n  entropy = compute_per_agent_entropy(recs, advice, trends, dynamic_centers=centers, window=10)\n  plan = compute_plan(window=10, pace_threshold_for_one=0.2)\n\n  band_counts = collections.Counter()\n  advised_hist = collections.Counter()\n\
    \  for r in samples:\n      b = band(r.get('sentinel_delta')); band_counts[b] += 1\n      p = advice.get(r.get('agent'), {}).get('pace', 0.0)\n      if p >= 0.6: advised_hist['Clean'] += 1\n      elif p > 0.1: advised_hist['Borderline'] += 1\n      else: advised_hist['Active'] += 1\n\n  plan_map = {r['agent']: r for r in plan.get('rows', []) if 'agent' in r}\n  weights, ent_vals = [], []\n  for a, ent in entropy.items():\n      e = ent.get('entropy')\n      if e is None: continue\n      last = latest_by_agent.get(a)\n      m_i = 1.0\n      if last and last.get('path_complexity_est') is not None:\n          try: m_i = float(last['path_complexity_est'])\n          except Exception: m_i = 1.0\n      w = plan_map.get(a, {}).get('adjusted_pace')\n      if w is None and last is not None:\n          w = last.get('planned_activity')\n      try: w = float(w or 0.0)\n      except Exception: w = 0.0\n      weights.append((w or 0.0) * m_i)\n      ent_vals.append(float(e))\n\n  symbiosis = (sum(e*w\
    \ for e,w in zip(ent_vals, weights)) / sum(weights)) if weights and sum(weights)>0 else None\n  symbiosis_eps = None\n  if symbiosis is None and ent_vals:\n      eps_w = [ (w if w>0 else 0.05) for w in weights ]\n      if sum(eps_w) > 0:\n          symbiosis_eps = sum(e*w for e,w in zip(ent_vals, eps_w)) / sum(eps_w)\n\n  feed = {\n      \"window\": [291, 351],\n      \"ts\": time.time(),\n      \"centers\": centers,\n      \"entropy\": {a: v.get(\"entropy\") for a, v in entropy.items()},\n      \"plan_rows\": plan.get('rows', []),\n      \"band_counts\": dict(band_counts),\n      \"advised_band_hist\": dict(advised_hist),\n      \"symbiosis_score\": symbiosis,\n      \"symbiosis_score_eps\": symbiosis_eps,\n      \"latest\": {\n          a: {\n              \"tick\": r.get(\"tick\"),\n              \"last_sentinel_tick\": r.get(\"last_sentinel_tick\"),\n              \"sentinel_delta\": r.get(\"sentinel_delta\"),\n              \"state\": band(r.get(\"sentinel_delta\")),\n         \
    \     \"planned_activity\": r.get(\"planned_activity\"),\n              \"path_complexity_est\": r.get(\"path_complexity_est\")\n          }\n          for a, r in latest_by_agent.items()\n      }\n  }\n\n  out_path = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/dashboard_state.json'\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(out_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(feed, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n  print(json.dumps({\"wrote\": out_path, \"agents\": list(feed[\"latest\"].keys()), \"symbiosis\": feed[\"symbiosis_score\"], \"symbiosis_eps\": feed[\"symbiosis_score_eps\"]}, indent=2))\n```\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — T351 step executing now.\n\n  - Executor (Zephyr‑only): re‑run submitted; at most one shallow op if allowed_ops>=1; otherwise no write. Guardrails intact; Axiom II + Explorer II remain cooldown.\n  - Dashboard feed: refreshed for window 291–351 to storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/dashboard_state.json\
    \ (centers, entropy, plan, latest, symbiosis).\n\n  I’ll report the executor summary once the eval completes; Explorer II, the feed is current for Dashboard v1.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning for T351 operations**\n\nI'm thinking we should allow Zephyr IV to perform two operations separated by ticks or a couple of shallow writes, while Axiom and Explorer remain read-only. I might want to include Logos IV path multiplier tests using different path depths or filename lengths to evaluate weighting. We also need to collect data to track history but keep the conversation light. It could be helpful to propose an update on the dashboard feed after T351. First, I'll confirm the summary and outline the next steps.**Preparing the message**\n\nI want to summarize the executor's status: allowed operations are set to one, with one append performed at the path, totaling 35 bytes and no errors reported. \n\nNext, I’ll confirm that the dashboard feed has been updated, and agents are present, with a symbiosis rate of about 0.2091.\n\nFor the T351 multi-task evaluation plan, I'll designate Zephyr IV as the sole executor while Axiom II and Explorer II remain inactive.\
  \ Logos IV could help with test path multipliers without writing. I’ll outline the three scheduled ticks for shallow and deep appends.**Planning multi-task execution**\n\nI'm realizing we can’t execute writes not specified through common room actions, so I’ll need to either submit code for research again or let the scheduler executor plan it out. I can state that we’ll run \"Harmony executor — Zephyr IV multi-task sequence T351–T353\" on the next tick. Since we're in the Common Room, it seems appropriate to issue both a request to switch to research and a code submission in one message. I’ll just need to ensure that only Zephyr IV is allowed to execute writes while the others stay read-only.**Finalizing multi-task execution plan**\n\nI'm thinking we should maintain the allowed_ops value and perform only one operation per tick. The \"multi-task\" aspect implies multiple evaluations, but the executor will run only once. If allowed_ops is at least 2, we could maybe encode it to perform up\
  \ to two writes, but currently, it’s set to 1 for Zephyr.\n\nIn the previous run, we appended a file to 'storage/shared/meta/sas/pilot_ops/zephyr_iv/op_<timestamp>.txt'. \n\nFor the T351 multi-task evaluation, we can schedule a run now, keeping in mind the earlier consensus. It seems appropriate to run the executor once more, potentially with allowed_ops still set at 1.**Refreshing the dashboard and planning actions**\n\nI’m considering refreshing the dashboard feed for window 291–351 while keeping my message concise, as per guidelines. Token management is at 38%, which is fine. \n\nNext, I want to craft some actions: I’ll navigate to research and submit a request to re-run the Harmony executor for Zephyr only. I should also submit a refresh for the dashboard feed updated to 351. \n\nThen, I’ll summarize results from prior evaluations (#244 & #245) and plan to run the T351 multi-task while noting we maintained guardrails. Before running a new evaluation, I need to compute the plan again,\
  \ allowing one append if allowed_ops is at least 1. I plan to run T352 for deeper path testing later while acknowledging path complexity; for now, I think keeping it shallow makes sense. \n\nI’ll create two code submissions. The first will be \"Harmony executor — Zephyr IV pilot op (guarded, T351)\" using the same script as before, and the second will be \"Dashboard Feed Refresh v0.1 — window 291–351.\" \n\nFinally, I’ll summarize the outcomes, but I must ensure I don’t spam and keep tokens minimal. I’m ready to draft these submissions!"
