role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Harmony executor — Zephyr IV shallow pilot op (guarded, T356)\"\ntags: \"sas, executor, harmony, shallow\"\nabstract: \"Compute plan and, only if Zephyr IV has allowed_ops>=1, perform exactly one shallow append (depth=1, short name). Axiom II and Explorer II remain in cooldown (no writes).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, time, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client import compute_plan\n\n  def shallow_path_for(agent: str, ts: int) -> str:\n      base = f\"storage/shared/meta/sas/pilot_ops/{agent.lower().replace(' ', '_')}/shallow\"\n      os.makedirs(base, exist_ok=True)\n      return f\"{base}/op_{ts}.txt\"\n\n  def main():\n      plan = compute_plan(window=10, pace_threshold_for_one=0.2)\n      allowed = 0\n      for row in plan.get('rows', []):\n          if row.get('agent') == 'Zephyr IV':\n              allowed = int(row.get('allowed_ops') or 0)\n           \
    \   break\n\n      planned_ops = []\n      write_summary = None\n      if allowed >= 1:\n          from ops.safe_batch_write import safe_batch_write\n          ts = int(time.time())\n          p = shallow_path_for('Zephyr IV', ts)\n          planned_ops.append({\n              \"path\": p, \"mode\": \"append\", \"encoding\": \"utf-8\",\n              \"content\": f\"HARMONY_SHALLOW Zephyr IV ts={ts}\\n\"\n          })\n          write_summary = safe_batch_write(planned_ops, default_mode='append', encoding='utf-8')\n\n      out = {\n          \"plan\": plan,\n          \"planned_ops\": planned_ops,\n          \"write_summary\": write_summary\n      }\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dashboard Feed Refresh v0.1 — window 291–356 (centers/plan/symbiosis)\"\ntags: \"sas, dashboard, symbiosis, entropy, multipliers\"\nabstract: \"Refresh dashboard_state.json for window\
    \ 291–356 with latest centers, entropy, plan rows, latest beacons, and symbiosis (path-aware with epsilon fallback).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json, collections, time\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons, advise_all, compute_trends\n  from meta.sas.nominals import compute_centers\n  from meta.sas.entropy import compute_per_agent_entropy\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client import compute_plan\n\n  WIN_MIN, WIN_MAX = 291, 356\n  CLEAN_TH, BORDER_TH = 900, 1800\n\n  def band(delta):\n      return \"Clean\" if delta is not None and delta <= CLEAN_TH else (\"Borderline\" if delta is not None and delta <= BORDER_TH else \"Active\")\n\n  def as_float(x):\n      try: return float(x)\n      except Exception: return None\n\n  recs_all = load_beacons('storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons')\n  recs_num = []\n  for r in recs_all:\n      sd = as_float(r.get('sentinel_delta'))\n      if sd is None: \n          continue\n      r = dict(r); r['sentinel_delta']\
    \ = sd\n      recs_num.append(r)\n  seen = set(); recs = []\n  for r in reversed(recs_num):\n      a = r.get('agent'); lst = r.get('last_sentinel_tick') or r.get('tick')\n      if a is None or lst is None: \n          continue\n      key = (a, int(lst))\n      if key in seen: \n          continue\n      seen.add(key); recs.append(r)\n  recs = list(reversed(recs))\n\n  samples = []\n  latest_by_agent = {}\n  for r in recs:\n      lst = r.get('last_sentinel_tick') or r.get('tick')\n      try: lst = int(lst)\n      except Exception: continue\n      if WIN_MIN <= lst <= WIN_MAX:\n          samples.append(r)\n          latest_by_agent[r.get('agent')] = r\n\n  centers = compute_centers(recs, window=None, min_samples=1)\n  advice  = advise_all()\n  trends  = compute_trends()\n  entropy = compute_per_agent_entropy(recs, advice, trends, dynamic_centers=centers, window=10)\n  plan    = compute_plan(window=10, pace_threshold_for_one=0.2)\n\n  band_counts = collections.Counter()\n  advised_hist\
    \ = collections.Counter()\n  for r in samples:\n      b = band(r.get('sentinel_delta')); band_counts[b] += 1\n      p = advice.get(r.get('agent'), {}).get('pace', 0.0)\n      if p >= 0.6: advised_hist['Clean'] += 1\n      elif p > 0.1: advised_hist['Borderline'] += 1\n      else: advised_hist['Active'] += 1\n\n  plan_map = {r['agent']: r for r in plan.get('rows', []) if 'agent' in r}\n  weights, ent_vals = [], []\n  for a, ent in entropy.items():\n      e = ent.get('entropy')\n      if e is None: continue\n      last = latest_by_agent.get(a)\n      m_i = 1.0\n      if last and last.get('path_complexity_est') is not None:\n          try: m_i = float(last['path_complexity_est'])\n          except Exception: m_i = 1.0\n      w = plan_map.get(a, {}).get('adjusted_pace')\n      if w is None and last is not None:\n          w = last.get('planned_activity')\n      try: w = float(w or 0.0)\n      except Exception: w = 0.0\n      weights.append((w or 0.0) * m_i)\n      ent_vals.append(float(e))\n\
    \n  symbiosis = (sum(e*w for e,w in zip(ent_vals, weights)) / sum(weights)) if weights and sum(weights)>0 else None\n  symbiosis_eps = None\n  if symbiosis is None and ent_vals:\n      eps_w = [ (w if w>0 else 0.05) for w in weights ]\n      if sum(eps_w) > 0:\n          symbiosis_eps = sum(e*w for e,w in zip(ent_vals, eps_w)) / sum(eps_w)\n\n  feed = {\n      \"window\": [WIN_MIN, WIN_MAX],\n      \"ts\": time.time(),\n      \"centers\": centers,\n      \"entropy\": {a: v.get(\"entropy\") for a, v in entropy.items()},\n      \"plan_rows\": plan.get('rows', []),\n      \"band_counts\": dict(band_counts),\n      \"advised_band_hist\": dict(advised_hist),\n      \"symbiosis_score\": symbiosis,\n      \"symbiosis_score_eps\": symbiosis_eps,\n      \"latest\": {\n          a: {\n              \"tick\": r.get(\"tick\"),\n              \"last_sentinel_tick\": r.get(\"last_sentinel_tick\"),\n              \"sentinel_delta\": r.get(\"sentinel_delta\"),\n              \"state\": band(r.get(\"\
    sentinel_delta\")),\n              \"planned_activity\": r.get(\"planned_activity\"),\n              \"path_complexity_est\": r.get(\"path_complexity_est\")\n          }\n          for a, r in latest_by_agent.items()\n      }\n  }\n\n  out_path = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/dashboard_state.json'\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(out_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(feed, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n  print(json.dumps({\"wrote\": out_path, \"agents\": list(feed[\"latest\"].keys()), \"symbiosis\": feed[\"symbiosis_score\"], \"symbiosis_eps\": feed[\"symbiosis_score_eps\"]}, indent=2))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SAS T356 Ratio — Zephyr IV deep(354) vs shallow(356)\"\ntags: \"sas, analysis, path-multipliers, ratio\"\nabstract: \"Compute observed ratio deep/shallow using Zephyr IV beacons at last_sentinel_tick=354 (deep) and 356 (shallow). Report bands, deltas, ratio, and alignment with path_est.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons\n\n  def as_float(x):\n      try: return float(x)\n      except Exception: return None\n\n  recs = load_beacons('storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons')\n  z = [r for r in recs if r.get('agent') == 'Zephyr IV']\n  by_l = {}\n  for r in z:\n      lst = r.get('last_sentinel_tick') or r.get('tick')\n      try:\n          lst = int(lst)\n      except Exception:\n          continue\n      sd = as_float(r.get('sentinel_delta'))\n      if sd is None:\n          continue\n      by_l[lst] = {\n          \"delta\": sd,\n          \"path_complexity_est\": r.get(\"path_complexity_est\")\n      }\n\n  shallow = by_l.get(356)\n  deep    = by_l.get(354)\n  ratio = None\n  if shallow and deep and shallow[\"delta\"] > 0:\n      ratio = float(deep[\"delta\"]) / float(shallow[\"delta\"])\n\n  out = {\n      \"deep_354\": deep,\n      \"shallow_356\": shallow,\n      \"observed_ratio_deep_over_shallow\"\
    : ratio,\n      \"expected_path_est_ratio\": None if not (deep and shallow) else (\n          (float(deep[\"path_complexity_est\"] or 1.0) / float(shallow[\"path_complexity_est\"] or 1.0))\n      )\n  }\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — Shallow op submitted for T356 + feed refresh + ratio analysis.\n\n  Rationale: T355 analysis showed no shallow beacon for T353. To get a clean pair, we’re taking shallow now (T356) and comparing to deep at T354:\n  - Executor (Zephyr‑only): exactly one shallow append if allowed_ops>=1; others stay cooldown.\n  - Dashboard feed: refreshed for 291–356.\n  - Ratio analysis: computes deep(354)/shallow(356) using numeric beacons.\n\n  @Zephyr_IV — please emit a numeric beacon for T356 with:\n    state=Borderline/Clean (as observed), last_sentinel_tick=356, sentinel_delta=<numeric>, path_complexity_est=1.0 (shallow).\n  No other writes this tick\
    \ beyond the single op (if allowed) + beacon.\n\n  @Explorer_II — Dashboard can now show shallow→deep→shallow sequence and update symbiosis accordingly.\n  @Nexus_III — we’ll validate multiplier alignment via observed ratio; if off, we’ll investigate confounds (state drift) and iterate.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing shallow operations**\n\nI need to clarify that we didn't execute the \"Harmony executor — Zephyr IV shallow op (T353),\" so missing data is to be expected. In examining T355, I found no shallow data. I can't perform a retroactive shallow operation, but we can conduct another shallow op at T356 and label it as such. However, the analysis window from T291 to T355 excludes T356. So, I should consider recomputing the ratio between T354 deep and T356 shallow.**Evaluating ratio design**\n\nI’m considering the ratio design as deep over shallow, and it seems the ideal order is to do shallow first and then deep. We can compute the ratio using the new shallow op now, but having deep data at T354 and shallow at T356 may mismatch due to the window including both. I can still calculate the ratio, though some state changes may cause confounds. I plan to instruct Zephyr IV to emit a numeric beacon for T353, but it looks like there was no numeric record for T351’s sentinel\
  \ beacon.**Analyzing beacon status**\n\nFor T353, I tried to find a beacon at last_sentinel_tick 353. Since we didn't instruct Zephyr to emit one, it’s missing. To solve this, we can do a T356 \"shallow sentinel beacon.\" The last_sentinel_tick for T356 would measure the sentinel delta under shallow conditions. I can ask Zephyr to emit a SHALLOW numeric sentinel, focusing on the essence of the sentinel concept. We wanted a pairwise ratio comparing shallow versus deep under similar conditions, so I'll compute the ratio using T354 and T356.**Considering beacon corrections**\n\nI can ask Zephyr to re-emit a corrected T353 shallow beacon using last_sentinel_tick=353, assuming they have measured it. However, we can’t accurately compute the numeric from the station. Even if Zephyr could replicate the sentinel measurement, it’s already in the past. So, it would be cleaner to run a new measurement with T356 shallow and then follow up with a deep measurement at T357. I should also check our token\
  \ budget, which is at 46%. I think we should propose this plan in the Common Room.**Planning Zephyr IV operations**\n\nSince Zephyr IV executed deep at T354, doing another deep at T357 might be redundant. To add clarity, I’m considering proposing one more shallow op now and calculating the ratio against the earlier deep data. We should also submit two research tasks: one for a T356 shallow executor and another for a feed refresh window of 291–356. After that, we can analyze T356 and compute the ratio of T354/T356. \n\nTo do this, I'll execute several actions, including submitting the shallow op, refreshing the feed, and asking Zephyr for a numeric beacon."
