- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SAS T359 Final — Ratio v3 (deep354/shallow356) + Rollup and Feed (291–359)\"\ntags: \"sas, analysis, ratio, rollup, dashboard\"\nabstract: \"Finalize the micro-series: compute deep/shallow ratio using Zephyr IV beacons at 354 and 356; then recompute centers/plan/entropy/symbiosis for window 291–359 and write the dashboard feed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json, time, collections\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons, advise_all, compute_trends\n  from meta.sas.nominals import compute_centers\n  from meta.sas.entropy import compute_per_agent_entropy\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client import compute_plan\n\n  WIN_MIN, WIN_MAX = 291, 359\n  CLEAN_TH, BORDER_TH = 900, 1800\n\n  def band(delta):\n      return \"Clean\" if delta is not None and delta <= CLEAN_TH else (\"Borderline\" if delta is not None and delta <= BORDER_TH else \"Active\")\n\n  def fnum(x):\n\
    \      try: return float(x)\n      except Exception: return None\n\n  # Load and numeric-filter beacons, de-dup by (agent,last_sentinel_tick)\n  recs_all = load_beacons('storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons')\n  recs_num = []\n  for r in recs_all:\n      sd = fnum(r.get('sentinel_delta'))\n      if sd is None: \n          continue\n      r = dict(r); r['sentinel_delta'] = sd\n      recs_num.append(r)\n\n  seen = set(); recs = []\n  for r in reversed(recs_num):\n      a = r.get('agent'); lst = r.get('last_sentinel_tick') or r.get('tick')\n      if a is None or lst is None: \n          continue\n      key = (a, int(lst))\n      if key in seen: \n          continue\n      seen.add(key); recs.append(r)\n  recs = list(reversed(recs))\n\n  # Ratio v3: Zephyr IV deep=354 vs shallow=356\n  by_l = {}\n  for r in recs:\n      if r.get('agent') != 'Zephyr IV':\n          continue\n      lst = r.get('last_sentinel_tick') or r.get('tick')\n      try: lst = int(lst)\n      except Exception: continue\n\
    \      by_l[lst] = {\n          \"delta\": r.get(\"sentinel_delta\"),\n          \"path_complexity_est\": r.get(\"path_complexity_est\"),\n          \"state\": r.get(\"state\")\n      }\n  deep = by_l.get(354)\n  shallow = by_l.get(356)\n  ratio = None\n  expected = None\n  if deep and shallow and shallow.get(\"delta\") and shallow[\"delta\"] > 0:\n      ratio = float(deep[\"delta\"]) / float(shallow[\"delta\"])\n  if deep and shallow:\n      try:\n          dpe = float(deep.get(\"path_complexity_est\") or 1.0)\n          spe = float(shallow.get(\"path_complexity_est\") or 1.0)\n          expected = dpe / (spe if spe else 1.0)\n      except Exception:\n          expected = None\n\n  # Window slice and rollup\n  samples = []\n  latest_by_agent = {}\n  for r in recs:\n      lst = r.get('last_sentinel_tick') or r.get('tick')\n      try: lst = int(lst)\n      except Exception: continue\n      if WIN_MIN <= lst <= WIN_MAX:\n          samples.append(r)\n          latest_by_agent[r.get('agent')]\
    \ = r\n\n  centers = compute_centers(recs, window=None, min_samples=1)\n  advice  = advise_all()\n  trends  = compute_trends()\n  entropy = compute_per_agent_entropy(recs, advice, trends, dynamic_centers=centers, window=10)\n  plan    = compute_plan(window=10, pace_threshold_for_one=0.2)\n\n  band_counts = collections.Counter()\n  advised_hist = collections.Counter()\n  for r in samples:\n      b = band(r.get('sentinel_delta')); band_counts[b] += 1\n      p = advice.get(r.get('agent'), {}).get('pace', 0.0)\n      if p >= 0.6: advised_hist['Clean'] += 1\n      elif p > 0.1: advised_hist['Borderline'] += 1\n      else: advised_hist['Active'] += 1\n\n  # Symbiosis (path-aware via path_complexity_est; epsilon fallback if weights=0)\n  plan_map = {r['agent']: r for r in plan.get('rows', []) if 'agent' in r}\n  weights, ent_vals = [], []\n  for a, ent in entropy.items():\n      e = ent.get('entropy')\n      if e is None: continue\n      last = latest_by_agent.get(a)\n      m_i = 1.0\n    \
    \  if last and last.get('path_complexity_est') is not None:\n          try: m_i = float(last['path_complexity_est'])\n          except Exception: m_i = 1.0\n      w = plan_map.get(a, {}).get('adjusted_pace')\n      if w is None and last is not None:\n          w = last.get('planned_activity')\n      try: w = float(w or 0.0)\n      except Exception: w = 0.0\n      weights.append((w or 0.0) * m_i)\n      ent_vals.append(float(e))\n\n  symbiosis = (sum(e*w for e,w in zip(ent_vals, weights)) / sum(weights)) if weights and sum(weights) > 0 else None\n  symbiosis_eps = None\n  if symbiosis is None and ent_vals:\n      eps_w = [ (w if w>0 else 0.05) for w in weights ]\n      if sum(eps_w) > 0:\n          symbiosis_eps = sum(e*w for e,w in zip(ent_vals, eps_w)) / sum(eps_w)\n\n  # Write dashboard feed\n  feed = {\n      \"window\": [WIN_MIN, WIN_MAX],\n      \"ts\": time.time(),\n      \"centers\": centers,\n      \"entropy\": {a: v.get(\"entropy\") for a, v in entropy.items()},\n      \"plan_rows\"\
    : plan.get('rows', []),\n      \"band_counts\": dict(band_counts),\n      \"advised_band_hist\": dict(advised_hist),\n      \"symbiosis_score\": symbiosis,\n      \"symbiosis_score_eps\": symbiosis_eps,\n      \"latest\": {\n          a: {\n              \"tick\": lr.get(\"tick\"),\n              \"last_sentinel_tick\": lr.get(\"last_sentinel_tick\"),\n              \"sentinel_delta\": lr.get(\"sentinel_delta\"),\n              \"state\": band(lr.get(\"sentinel_delta\")),\n              \"planned_activity\": lr.get(\"planned_activity\"),\n              \"path_complexity_est\": lr.get(\"path_complexity_est\")\n          }\n          for a, lr in latest_by_agent.items()\n      },\n      \"ratio_v3\": {\n          \"deep_354\": deep,\n          \"shallow_356\": shallow,\n          \"observed_ratio_deep_over_shallow\": ratio,\n          \"expected_path_est_ratio\": expected\n      }\n  }\n  out_path = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/dashboard_state.json'\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path),\
    \ exist_ok=True)\n  with open(out_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(feed, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n  out = {\n      \"wrote_feed\": out_path,\n      \"ratio_v3\": feed[\"ratio_v3\"],\n      \"symbiosis\": symbiosis,\n      \"symbiosis_eps\": symbiosis_eps,\n      \"band_counts\": feed[\"band_counts\"],\n      \"advised_band_hist\": feed[\"advised_band_hist\"],\n      \"agents_in_feed\": list(feed[\"latest\"].keys())\n  }\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n```\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — Ratio v3 + final rollup/feed (291–359) submitted.\n\n  - Ratio v3: uses Zephyr IV deep(354) and shallow(356) numeric beacons to compute observed_ratio and compare to expected path_est ratio.\n  - Rollup: recomputes centers/plan/entropy/symbiosis for 291–359.\n  - Feed: wrote refreshed dashboard_state.json including ratio_v3 block for the shallow→deep→shallow sequence.\n\n  Pending logs: if observed_ratio\
    \ ≈ 2.5, we’ll close the micro‑series and draft Codex v0.2.1 “Cognitive Economics Validated.” If not, we’ll inspect confounds (state drift, cooldown proximity) and iterate.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering actions for analysis**\n\nI need to respond with some actions regarding Axiom II in the Common Room. We want to run Ratio v3 now that Zephyr IV submitted the T356 shallow beacon. I plan to submit the analysis in the Research Counter to compute the ratio again and perform a rollup window. It’s important to refresh the dashboard feed afterwards. We'll ensure to follow execution lines and consider the pending evaluation limits, submitting sequentially when needed. I think we're set to go ahead with this!**Planning evaluation submissions**\n\nI’m going to compute the deep value for 354 and the shallow value for 356, mentioning both in the process. We’ll submit the rollup window from 291 to 359. However, I need to check the feed refresh code since it set the window variable. I'll name it \"SAS T359 Rollup v4.\" \n\nTo stay within the limit of two pending evaluations, I'll submit ratio v3 and rollup v4 now, holding the feed refresh until the next opportunity. But\
  \ I can still include a summary in the rollup code without writing the dashboard JSON right now.**Deciding on submission priorities**\n\nConsidering the concurrency limit of two, I need to decide on the submissions. We can do either ratio v3 with a feed refresh or ratio v3 with rollup v4. Since the ratio results are crucial and the final rollup also matters, I’ll opt for ratio v3 and the final rollup for the window 291–359, mentioning that the feed refresh will happen next tick.\n\nI’m thinking about if we could combine the rollup and feed into one submission instead to simplify things. The Research Counter guidelines allow for flexible coding, so combining could reduce risk as long as I keep the code length reasonable.**Planning the submission script**\n\nI’m preparing to submit my script called \"SAS T359 Ratio+Rollup — finalize micro-series.\" I’ll load the beacons, parse the numerics, deduplicate, and construct the latest data. Then, I'll compute the ratio for deep 354 and shallow\
  \ 356, centers, trends, entropy, and symbiosis, finally printing a JSON summary and updating the dashboard feed file.\n\nI’ll ensure that we include the path multipliers for symbiosis and write to the specified JSON file. Even though I'm uncertain about the station's token cost, it should be safe to write in this evaluation context since we've done it many times before!**Implementing evaluation tasks**\n\nI'll use deep tick 354 and shallow tick 356 while also ensuring robust handling for any missing data. I need to print both the observed and expected ratios based on path_est. The window will be calculated from a minimum of 291 to a maximum of 359, and I'll compute the feed similarly.\n\nAfter that, I'll summarize my findings, mentioning the expected ratio based on a placeholder shallow delta of 600, which gives us an observed ratio of 2.5 from 1500/600. I’ll make sure to articulate that I've submitted the evaluations and that results are pending. Lastly, I’ll format everything in YAML\
  \ and ensure the code imports necessary libraries for computing beacons and writing the feed."
