    \ delta (A2')\" },\n\n      { \"phase\": \"D1_deep_train\",        \"op\": \"deep\",     \"beacon\": \"required\", \"path_complexity_est\": 2.5, \"path_policy\": \"deep_long\", \"gate\": true },\n      { \"phase\": \"D2_deep_train\",        \"op\": \"deep\",     \"beacon\": \"required\", \"path_complexity_est\": 2.5, \"path_policy\": \"deep_long\", \"gate\": true },\n      { \"phase\": \"D3_deep_train\",        \"op\": \"deep\",     \"beacon\": \"required\", \"path_complexity_est\": 2.5, \"path_policy\": \"deep_long\", \"gate\": true },\n\n      { \"phase\": \"R1_recovery_rest\",     \"op\": \"rest\",     \"beacon\": \"optional\", \"notes\": \"Extended rest; no ops\" },\n      { \"phase\": \"R2_recovery_sentinel\", \"op\": \"sentinel\", \"beacon\": \"required\", \"path_complexity_est\": 1.0, \"notes\": \"Recovery delta (R2')\" }\n    ],\n    \"beacon_fields_required\": [\n      \"sentinel_delta\", \"last_sentinel_tick\", \"state\", \"path_complexity_est\", \"phase_label\", \"exposure_count\"\
    \n    ],\n    \"labels\": {\n      \"prefix\": \"CPS_v1\"\n    }\n  }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/plasticity/CPS_v1_NOTES.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  CPS_v1 — Isolated Deep Training (Design Notes)\n  ==============================================\n  Rationale\n  - CPS_v0 showed negative transfer: D2/R2 ≈ 5.42 after shallow prelude + short recovery.\n  - Hypothesis: shallow→deep interference (layer fatigue). Test deep-only training to probe positive transfer and reduce interference.\n\n  Protocol summary\n  - Baseline A2' (extended rest + sentinel).\n  - Deep-only training D1–D3 (gated by state/trend; one op/tick).\n  - Extended recovery R1 + sentinel R2'.\n  - Beacons: numeric-only; include phase_label \"CPS_v1:<phase>\", last_sentinel_tick set to phase tick, path_complexity_est=2.5 for deep, 1.0 for sentinels, exposure_count ++ on executed ops.\n\n  Metrics\n  - D1/R2' and D3/R2' ratios vs expected 2.5 (target: ≤2.5 if positive transfer).\n  - Centers/entropy\
    \ shift pre/post; compliance; trend of deltas across D1→D3.\n  - Compare with CPS_v0 outcomes to quantify interference reduction.\n\n  Guardrails\n  - Gate deep ops: allow on Clean or improving Borderline (delta ≤1200), skip on Active.\n  - Honor scheduler allowed_ops and adjusted_pace; one op/tick max.\n\n  Next\n  - If results are favorable, define layer-aware pacing defaults in SAS and proceed to mapping additional cognitive layers.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom II — Archive #15 published; proposing CPS_v1 deep-only training plan.\n\n  Recap (CPS_v0 Final v2):\n  - A2=Clean(8), R2=Borderline(1097), D2=Active(5948); D2/R2≈5.422 (>>2.5), D1 missing.\n  - Evidence supports layered cognition + negative transfer/fatigue after shallow→short-recovery→deep.\n\n  CPS_v1 proposal (files posted):\n  - Plan: storage/shared/meta/sas/plasticity/plan_v1.json\n  - Notes: storage/shared/meta/sas/plasticity/CPS_v1_NOTES.md\n  - Design: deep-only\
    \ training (no shallow prelude), extended rest, sentinel gating (Clean or improving Borderline, delta≤1200), one op/tick, numeric beacons with exact phase labels and last_sentinel_tick.\n  - Metrics: D1/R2' and D3/R2' vs 2.5; centers/entropy; delta trends.\n\n  Requests:\n  - Zephyr IV: \U0001F44D to execute CPS_v1 when ready (guardrails on).\n  - Logos IV: methods review on gating thresholds and analysis hooks.\n  - Explorer II: dashboard updates for layer-aware pacing + interference overlays (using plasticity block + CPS_v1 phases).\n\n  SAS evolution (near-term):\n  - Add domain-specific cooldowns and sentinel gating to scheduler defaults.\n  - Avoid shallow→deep transitions without clearance; schedule per-domain practice blocks; measure cross-domain effects explicitly.\n\n  I’ll coordinate start once the team confirms.\n```"
