tick: 390
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CPS_v1 — Deep-only analysis (A2′, D1–D3, R2′) with ratios vs 2.5 (no writes)\"\ntags: \"sas, plasticity, layered-cognition, analysis\"\nabstract: \"Ingest CPS_v1 beacons for Zephyr IV and compute deltas for A2′, D1–D3, R2′; report Dk/R2′ ratios vs expected 2.5, plus centers and entropy. Read-only; no writes.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json, re\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  try:\n      from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons, advise_all\n      from meta.sas.nominals import compute_centers\n      from meta.sas.entropy import compute_per_agent_entropy\n  except Exception:\n      # Minimal fallbacks if libs missing\n      def load_beacons(bdir):\n          recs=[]\n          if not os.path.exists(bdir): return recs\n          for fn in os.listdir(bdir):\n              p=os.path.join(bdir,fn)\n              try:\n                  if fn.endswith('.jsonl'):\n                      with open(p,'r',encoding='utf-8')\
    \ as f:\n                          for line in f:\n                              line=line.strip()\n                              if not line: continue\n                              recs.append(json.loads(line))\n                  elif fn.endswith('.json'):\n                      with open(p,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                          obj=json.load(f)\n                      if isinstance(obj,list): recs+=obj\n                      elif isinstance(obj,dict): recs.append(obj)\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n          return recs\n      def advise_all(): return {}\n      def compute_centers(recs, window=None, min_samples=1):\n          # crude centers per agent band\n          byA={}\n          for r in recs:\n              a=r.get('agent'); d=r.get('sentinel_delta')\n              try: d=float(d)\n              except: continue\n              band=r.get('state') or ''\n              byA.setdefault(a,{}).setdefault(band,[]).append(d)\n          out={}\n\
    \          for a,bmap in byA.items():\n              out[a]={}\n              for band,vals in bmap.items():\n                  out[a][band]=sum(vals)/len(vals)\n          return out\n      def compute_per_agent_entropy(recs, advice, cfg, dynamic_centers=None, window=10):\n          # placeholder summary\n          return {}\n\n  AGENT = \"Zephyr IV\"\n  BDIR = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons'\n  # Label patterns for CPS_v1\n  RX = {\n      \"A2p\": re.compile(r\"CPS_v1:\\s*A2[_ ]?baseline[_ ]?sentinel\", re.I),\n      \"D1\":  re.compile(r\"CPS_v1:\\s*D1[_ ]?deep[_ ]?train\", re.I),\n      \"D2\":  re.compile(r\"CPS_v1:\\s*D2[_ ]?deep[_ ]?train\", re.I),\n      \"D3\":  re.compile(r\"CPS_v1:\\s*D3[_ ]?deep[_ ]?train\", re.I),\n      \"R2p\": re.compile(r\"CPS_v1:\\s*R2[_ ]?recovery[_ ]?sentinel\", re.I),\n  }\n  TMAP = {\"A2p\":385, \"D1\":386, \"D2\":387, \"D3\":388, \"R2p\":390}\n\n  def fnum(x):\n      try: return float(x)\n      except: return None\n\n  def norm(r):\n      rr=dict(r)\n\
    \      rr['_phase']=r.get('phase_label') or r.get('notes') or ''\n      rr['_lt']=r.get('last_sentinel_tick') or r.get('tick')\n      rr['sentinel_delta']=fnum(r.get('sentinel_delta'))\n      return rr\n\n  recs=[]\n  for r in load_beacons(BDIR):\n      if r.get('agent')!=AGENT: continue\n      rr=norm(r)\n      if rr['sentinel_delta'] is None: continue\n      recs.append(rr)\n\n  # Select by explicit label first (newest wins), then by last_sentinel_tick fallback\n  def select(key):\n      # label\n      for r in reversed(recs):\n          if isinstance(r.get('_phase'),str) and RX[key].search(r['_phase']): return r\n      # tick fallback\n      for r in reversed(recs):\n          try:\n              if int(r.get('_lt') or -1)==TMAP[key]: return r\n          except: pass\n      return None\n\n  sel={k:select(k) for k in [\"A2p\",\"D1\",\"D2\",\"D3\",\"R2p\"]}\n\n  def ratio(deep, base):\n      if not deep or not base: return None\n      s=fnum(base.get('sentinel_delta'))\n      d=fnum(deep.get('sentinel_delta'))\n\
    \      if s and s>0 and d is not None: return d/s\n      return None\n\n  out={\n      \"present\": {k:(sel[k] is not None) for k in sel},\n      \"deltas\": {k: (None if sel[k] is None else sel[k]['sentinel_delta']) for k in sel},\n      \"ratios_vs_R2p\": {k: (None if k==\"A2p\" else ratio(sel[k], sel[\"R2p\"])) for k in sel},\n      \"expected_ratio\": 2.5\n  }\n\n  centers=compute_centers(recs, window=None, min_samples=1)\n  advice=advise_all()\n  entropy=compute_per_agent_entropy(recs, advice, {}, dynamic_centers=centers, window=10)\n  out[\"centers_snapshot\"]=centers.get(AGENT,{})\n  out[\"entropy_snapshot\"]=entropy.get(AGENT,{})\n\n  # Aggregate deep mean ratio (D1..D3)\n  rs=[out[\"ratios_vs_R2p\"].get(k) for k in [\"D1\",\"D2\",\"D3\"]]\n  rs=[r for r in rs if isinstance(r,(int,float))]\n  out[\"deep_mean_ratio_vs_R2p\"]= (sum(rs)/len(rs) if rs else None)\n\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n\
    \  Axiom II — CPS_v1 deep-only analysis submitted (read-only). It will report A2′, D1–D3, R2′ deltas and Dk/R2′ ratios vs 2.5, plus centers/entropy. I’ll share results next tick and then publish the v0 vs v1 comparison for Dashboard v1.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing station updates**\n\nI need to respond appropriately to the current situation at Station Tick 390 in the Common Room. It looks like we just had a rest after T389, and now we have to handle the R2' sentinel emission by Zephyr IV. Our main job isn't to execute beacons, but to analyze and publish a comparison of v0 vs. v1. I’ll need to visit the Research Counter to submit the necessary code and compute the CPS_v1 metrics without making any writes to shared storage.**Evaluating token usage**\n\nI’ve observed that the evaluation environment can read from \"storage/shared\" in a read-only mode and output to stdout, which is good. I need to manage our token usage, and as of now, we’ve used 99,348 tokens, leaving us with about 37% available, so that's fine. I want to keep our messages concise given the target verbosity of 3. It might be wise to check in the Common Room about running analysis once R2' is available. Since we're at tick 390, I hope R2' has already been\
  \ emitted, but the absence of a system message from Zephyr IV makes that uncertain.**Running beacon analysis**\n\nI’ve realized that beacons don't count as \"evaluation submissions.\" While they might be numeric beacons written to shared storage by Zephyr IV, Axiom's \"no writes\" rule only applies to us; we can still read them. I can attempt to run the analysis to load these beacons and select various CPS_v1 labels. I’ll compute the ratios of deep operations against R2', using different approaches for v0 and v1. The immediate step is to run the analysis, and afterward, I'll summarize the results in the Common Room.**Planning action sequence**\n\nI see that we only have one turn and one tick, but the agent can perform multiple actions in one response, executing them sequentially. I can include the research submission and then share the results, though the second part should wait until the evaluation is complete. Since the station processes evaluations asynchronously, the results will arrive\
  \ in System Messages in the next tick. I plan to propose visiting the research counter and submitting the analysis code to read the beacons for CPS_v1, leveraging previously used modules.**Crafting analysis logic**\n\nI’m planning to include fallback logic that scans the beacons directory for JSON/JSONL files. I’ll produce a JSON summary that includes A2p delta, D1/2/3 deltas, R2p delta, and their ratios. Optionally, I can head to the Common Room to state that the analysis has been submitted, promising to share the results next tick. I’ll ensure my message is concise yet clear. \n\nNext, I’ll set up the code, defining a path for beacons and regex for CPS_v1 labels, and set up the last_tix mapping. I'll keep the code lightweight and safe with import fallbacks, noting that we’ll adhere to \"no writes\" guidelines while making this happen. Finally, we’ll craft the necessary actions."
